{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c525","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a182c7-1fa3-7740-b1c6-efc1a8b254a1"},"sequence":237,"recorded_at":1780531400000469,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"01a182c7-21ae-7563-b8aa-8495f4c7e6b2","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"command_id":"01a182c7-21ae-7563-b8aa-8495f4c7e6b2","event":{"chunk":"package-lock.json:2324:        \"@playwright/test\": \"^1.51.1\",\ndata/music/labels.json:346:      \"durationSec\": 291.58\napp/globals.css:63:  text-indent: 1.5em;\napp/player.tsx:319:          <rect x=\"11.5\" y=\"3\" width=\"2\" height=\"10\" rx=\"0.5\" />\napp/player.tsx:340:              strokeWidth=\"1.5\"\napp/player.tsx:348:              strokeWidth=\"1.5\"\ndocs/reviews/10.md:59:   (\"1.5 s for hard cuts\"). The code deleted `gatedEvaluate`, so\ndocs/reviews/05.md:14:   Problem: `toggle` pauses only the live element. For 1.5 s after a track change the standby element is the audible one, so pressing pause in that window sets state to paused while audio keeps playing.\ndocs/reviews/05.md:114:3. First press double start: confirmed, conditional on a scheduler switch before first press setting `fadeSec` to 3 or 1.5. Common case (`fadeSec` 0) still reassigns `src` twice.\ndocs/reviews/05.md:124:- Scheduler: first track immediate, 20 s dwell with newest-pending-wins, 0.07 margin boundary tested both sides, 45 s min-track with 1.5 s hard-cut exception, null scene promotes without switching.\ndocs/reviews/external-opus-music-selection.md:79:| Crossfade | 3 s normally, 1.5 s for hard cuts; respect reduced-motion only for visuals, not audio |\ndocs/spikes.md:11:| (a) `response_format: url` | 200 | 31.5 s | 982152 | 1600x1600 VP8X | 31245 / 2459 |\ndocs/spikes.md:45:| poppy field | 103 ms | suspenso 0.95 | 2.08, norm 0.52 (0.66) | 1.52, norm 0.38 (0.52) | 848 / 117 |\ndocs/tasks/05-contracts-reader.md:117:playing --track change--> crossfading --1.5s--> playing\ndocs/tasks/05-contracts-reader.md:122:Two `audio` elements fade against each other on change over about 1.5 s, then the old one pauses. `prefers-reduced-motion` sets the fade to 0. Choice: plain audio elements with a volume ramp instead of Web Audio because nothing here needs decoding or filtering, and native elements keep codec and loop behavior free. Loop is on. Audio starts only after the user presses play, which satisfies autoplay rules; track swaps before first press only change `src`. Volume slider sets both elements. UI motion stays under 200 ms per tokens; the audio fade is not UI motion. Controls are real buttons with labels, visible focus, and full keyboard use. The bar shows the track label and the active scene title.\ndocs/contracts.md:52:with no paragraph gaps and a 1.5em first-line indent on following\ndocs/contracts.md:310:credits for today are used up. Come back tomorrow, or bring your own\ndocs/contracts.md:325:counter per UTC day under `DAILY_SPEND_CAP_USD` (default 1.5, 48 h key\nagent-logs/04-impl.jsonl:408:{\"schema_version\":1,\"id\":\"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c67b\",\"stream\":{\"kind\":\"session\",\"id\":\"01a17ee0-a092-7f93-b8fa-5add1afe57e5\"},\"sequence\":408,\"recorded_at\":1780531400000811,\"record_type\":\"event\",\"durability\":\"durable\",\"causation_id\":\"01a17ee0-a1d9-7863-b0fc-80f17b6c0588\",\"payload_type\":\"task.lifecycle.output\",\"payload_schema_version\":1,\"payload\":{\"command_id\":\"01a17ee0-a1d9-7863-b0fc-80f17b6c0588\",\"event\":{\"chunk\":\"{\\n  \\\"chunk_id\\\": \\\"exec-7-1\\\",\\n  \\\"command\\\": \\\"npm install 2>&1 | tail -5\\\",\\n  \\\"description\\\": \\\"Install dev dependencies with npm\\\",\\n  \\\"exit_code\\\": 0,\\n  \\\"terminal_status\\\": \\\"completed\\\",\\n  \\\"output\\\": \\\"npm warn install-scripts 2 packages have install scripts not yet covered by allowScripts:\\\\nnpm warn install-scripts   esbuild@0.28.2 (postinstall: node install.js)\\\\nnpm warn install-scripts   esbuild@0.21.5 (postinstall: node install.js)\\\\nnpm warn install-scripts\\\\nnpm warn install-scripts Run `npm install-scripts ls` to review, or `npm install-scripts approve <pkg>` to allow.\\\\n\\\",\\n  \\\"original_output_bytes\\\": 375,\\n  \\\"original_output_tokens\\\": 94,\\n  \\\"truncated\\\": false\\n}\",\"final_result\":true,\"kind\":\"output\",\"task_id\":\"01a17ee0-ff07-7a20-b5bd-c2c83d5d49b1\"},\"kind\":\"task_lifecycle\",\"run_stream\":{\"id\":\"01a17ee0-a1d9-7863-b0fc-80f17b6c0588\",\"kind\":\"run\"},\"task_id\":\"01a17ee0-ff07-7a20-b5bd-c2c83d5d49b1\",\"task_stream\":{\"id\":\"01a17ee0-ff07-7a20-b5bd-c2c83d5d49b1\",\"kind\":\"task\"}}}\nagent-logs/04-impl.jsonl:410:{\"schema_version\":1,\"id\":\"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c67f\",\"stream\":{\"kind\":\"session\",\"id\":\"01a17ee0-a092-7f93-b8fa-5add1afe57e5\"},\"sequence\":410,\"recorded_at\":1780531400000815,\"record_type\":\"event\",\"durability\":\"durable\",\"causation_id\":\"01a17ee0-a1d9-7863-b0fc-80f17b6c0588\",\"payload_type\":\"tool.result\",\"payload_schema_version\":1,\"payload\":{\"call_id\":\"call_01a17ee0fa74737d9bd5c27bfa2ce0dc\",\"command_id\":\"01a17ee0-a1d9-7863-b0fc-80f17b6c0588\",\"correlation_facts\":{\"outcome\":\"success\",\"tool_name\":\"bash\"},\"kind\":\"tool_result\",\"run_stream\":{\"id\":\"01a17ee0-a1d9-7863-b0fc-80f17b6c0588\",\"kind\":\"run\"},\"text\":\"{\\n  \\\"chunk_id\\\": \\\"exec-7-1\\\",\\n  \\\"command\\\": \\\"npm install 2>&1 | tail -5\\\",\\n  \\\"description\\\": \\\"Install dev dependencies with npm\\\",\\n  \\\"exit_code\\\": 0,\\n  \\\"terminal_status\\\": \\\"completed\\\",\\n  \\\"output\\\": \\\"npm warn install-scripts 2 packages have install scripts not yet covered by allowScripts:\\\\nnpm warn install-scripts   esbuild@0.28.2 (postinstall: node install.js)\\\\nnpm warn install-scripts   esbuild@0.21.5 (postinstall: node install.js)\\\\nnpm warn install-scripts\\\\nnpm warn install-scripts Run `npm install-scripts ls` to review, or `npm install-scripts approve <pkg>` to allow.\\\\n\\\",\\n  \\\"original_output_bytes\\\": 375,\\n  \\\"original_output_tokens\\\": 94,\\n  \\\"truncated\\\": false\\n}\"}}\nagent-logs/06-review.jsonl:52:{\"schema_version\":1,\"id\":\"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c3b3\",\"stream\":{\"kind\":\"session\",\"id\":\"01a18013-5db9-7772-9613-fed1b45db42e\"},\"sequence\":52,\"recorded_at\":1780531400000099,\"record_type\":\"event\",\"durability\":\"durable\",\"causation_id\":\"01a18013-60b1-7551-82e2-1b1f3ccd850e\",\"payload_type\":\"task.lifecycle.output\",\"payload_schema_version\":1,\"payload\":{\"command_id\":\"01a18013-60b1-7551-82e2-1b1f3ccd850e\",\"event\":{\"chunk\":\"Read text file `docs/reviews/05.md`.\\n1|# Review: task 5 contracts and scene reader\\n2|\\n3|Verdict: fix finding 1 first. The reader renders and plays, but slow scrolling never moves the music to the next scene. Findings 2 to 6 should land in the same pass; 7 to 11 are nits.\\n4|\\n5|What this change does: adds the module contracts in `docs/contracts.md`, pure track selection and manifest parsing in `core/music.ts`, the slim reader model in `core/reader.ts`, a server-only Oz loader in `server/books.ts`, and the client reader (`app/reader.tsx`, `app/active-scene.ts`, `app/player.tsx`) with a two-track placeholder manifest in `public/music/`.\\n6|\\n7|## Findings\\n8|\\n9|1. **Slow scroll down never advances the active scene** (blocker), `app/reader.tsx:107-119`, `app/active-scene.ts:10-25`.\\n10|   Problem: the observer callback scores only the changed entries. A new scene enters the 5 percent band from below with its top under the reading line, so `pickActiveScene` skips it. Its top then crosses the line with no further callback (intersection status does not change), and when the old scene exits, the old entry is filtered out and the result falls back to current. The next scene is adopted only when its top is already above the line at entry, which is the scroll-up direction plus jumps, not scroll-down.\\n11|   Fix: use entries only as a trigger and re-snapshot all sections with live rects on each callback, as the mount path already does. Derive the hit flag from rect versus band in the snapshot mapper.\\n12|\\n13|2. **Pause during a crossfade leaves the incoming element playing** (should-fix), `app/player.tsx:61-80`.\\n14|   Problem: `toggle` pauses only the live element. For 1.5 s after a track change the standby element is the audible one, so pressing pause in that window sets state to paused while audio keeps playing.\\n15|   Fix: pause both refs in `toggle`, or keep the fading pair in one ref both handlers use.\\n16|\\n17|3. **Volume sits in the track-effect deps and restarts fades** (should-fix), `app/player.tsx:28-59`.\\n18|   Problem: every slider tick re-runs the track effect. While paused the early return does not apply (live is paused), so each tick reassigns `standby.src` and flips `liveRef`. Mid-fade it also reassigns the incoming `src`, which reloads that track from zero, and starts a fresh interval.\\n19|   Fix: drop `volume` from the deps, read it through a ref inside the fade, and return early when the live element already carries the track `src` regardless of paused state.\\n20|\\n21|4. **Validator accepts NaN vector entries** (should-fix), `core/music.ts:34-37`.\\n22|   Problem: `isVector8` checks `typeof` only, and `typeof NaN` is `number`. A NaN entry passes `parseManifest`, then poisons the cosine score and the sort order for that track.\\n23|   Fix: require `Number.isFinite` for each of the 8 values, one word in the same check.\\n24|\\n25|5. **Tests skip the behaviors the brief asked about** (should-fix), `core/music.test.ts`, `app/reader.tsx:36-61`.\\n26|   Problem: no test covers `nextAlternative` with a null scene, `selectTrack` with an excluded current track, the skip override held until the scene change and then used as current, or reselection when the manifest lands after the first scene. The observer wiring has no test beyond the pure picker.\\n27|   Fix: add the three core cases (null scene alternative, excluded current, excluded all) and pull `applyScene` into a pure helper beside `active-scene.ts` with two tests: override as base on scene change, cleared after.\\n28|\\n29|6. **Doc says the reader consumes `scenes.json`, code never reads it** (should-fix), `docs/contracts.md:11-20`, `server/books.ts:9-17`.\\n30|   Problem: `loadOzBook` reads `book.json` plus `analysis.json` only, which is fine because analysis carries every scene field, but the contract lists `scenes.json` as an input the reader consumes.\\n31|   Fix: name `analysis.json` as the scene source and `scenes.json` as the pipeline intermediate it mirrors, in one sentence.\\n32|\\n33|7. **Tie-break repeats an index scan per comparison** (nit), `core/music.ts:96-99`.\\n34|   Problem: the comparator calls `manifest.tracks.indexOf` on each tie. Sort is already stable, so ties follow manifest order without it.\\n35|   Fix: delete the tie branch and return the diff.\\n36|\\n37|8. **Two `SceneEmotion` types with different shapes** (nit), `core/music.ts:22-26`, `core/types.ts:78-83`.\\n38|   Problem: `core/music.ts` exports `SceneEmotion` as `{ vector, intensity, tempo }` while `core/types.ts` uses the same name for `{ jev, muse_override, final, error }`. Each reads fine alone; importing both invites the wrong one.\\n39|   Fix: rename the music one to `SceneSignal` or reuse an inline param type.\\n40|\\n41|9. **Snapshot helper takes a flag it never varies** (nit), `app/reader.tsx:31, 101-106`.\\n42|   Problem: `snapshot(hit)` is called once with `true`, and `byId.current` is rebuilt on every render.\\n43|   Fix: delete the parameter and build the map with `useMemo` on `scenes`.\\n44|\\n45|10. **Reduced-motion choice never updates** (nit), `app/player.tsx:26`.\\n46|    Problem: `matchMedia` runs per render with no listener, so flipping the OS setting mid session keeps the old fade until a rerender for another reason.\\n47|    Fix: read it once in state with a change listener, or leave it; the wrongness lasts one session at most.\\n48|\\n49|11. **Track swap mid-fade restarts from partial volumes** (nit), `app/player.tsx:43-56`.\\n50|    Problem: the cleanup clears the old interval but leaves the old live element at partial volume, and the new run fades from there while the incoming `src` is replaced. Playback converges, only the fade curve kinks.\\n51|    Fix: nothing required once finding 3 lands; note it only if the effect is reworked anyway.\\n52|\\n53|## Checked and fine\\n54|\\n55|- Core purity: no `process.env`, `node:` imports, `fetch`, or `fs` in `core/` outside tests. Import direction holds: `app/page.tsx` imports `server/books.ts`, client files import only `core/` and siblings, `server/books.ts` starts with `import 'server-only'`.\\n56|- Client payload: only scene ids, titles, and emotion triples pass to `Reader`. `buildReaderModel` spreads `final` (`vector`, `intensity`, `tempo`) and drops `jev`, `muse_override`, provenance. The reader test asserts both internals are absent.\\n57|- Image and chat types match the spec: `{ bookId, textVersion, firstN, lastN }` to `{ url }`, and `{ bookId, textVersion, positionN, spoilerMode, messages }` with `{ role, text }` messages. Contract only, no routes.\\n58|- Manifest trust boundary: the client parses every fetch with `parseManifest`, which rejects unknown versions, missing fields, short vectors, out-of-range numbers, and non-`/music/` non-https `src`. Bad drop-ins fail loudly.\\n59|- CSP unchanged and sufficient: `media-src 'self' blob:` covers the placeholder clips, `connect-src 'self'` covers the manifest fetch. Both docs note remote https tracks need a `media-src` edit.\\n60|- Reading line consistent with the band: the band spans 30 to 35 percent of viewport height, the line sits at one third, inside the band. Short scenes still cross it because sections span their paragraphs.\\n61|- Swap guide: `public/music/README.md` replaces files plus manifest plus version bump, names `parseManifest` as the shape check, and carries the CC-BY-NC non-commercial note. Swap needs no code change.\\n62|- Design: styles use tokens only (all names exist in `app/tokens.css`), accent is Meta blue on borders and focus, no purple or gradients, controls are real buttons and inputs with labels and visible focus, no UI transition over 200 ms (audio fade is not UI motion).\\n63|- Prose: `docs/contracts.md` and the README are short, sentence case, no filler or banned words.\\n64|- Runs: `npm test` 63/63 across 14 files, `npm run typecheck` clean, `npm run build` clean with `/` prerendered static.\\n65|\\n66|## Not checked\\n67|\\n68|- Audible playback, real scroll behavior, and screen-reader pass were not run; the observer finding rests on reading plus band math, not a browser session. Live manifest fetch against the built server was not repeated.\\n69|\\n70|## Round 2\\n71|\\n72|What this change does: the fix pass answers findings 1 to 10, adds manifest v2 with hand-labeled emotions, a pure scheduler with dwell/hysteresis/min-track/hard-cut, same-emotion Next, and a two-element player rewrite with loop crossfades and attribution. The rules all land. Three player/scheduler defects do not.\\n73|\\n74|### Must fix\\n75|\\n76|1. **Reader skip choice reverts on the same scene** (breaks Martin's rule), `core/music-schedule.ts:60-100, 151-166`.\\n77|   Problem: `evaluateSwitch` never reads `overrideId`, and `tickScheduler` re-runs it every second. After Change track the override is a dead field: it is set in `requestNext` (`music-schedule.ts:185-186`) and cleared in `promote`, but nothing checks it.\\n78|   Case (run against the real scheduler): scene pure tristeza, tracks pure/bland tristeza plus calm; Next moves pure to bland with gap 0.145, then `tickScheduler` at 45 s after the press switches back to pure on the same scene, stale `overrideId: bland` still set. Gaps at or above `hardCutMargin` revert within one second instead. The committed fixture hides this only because its same-emotion gaps sit below `switchMargin`.\\n79|   Fix: in `tickScheduler`, when there is no pending scene and `overrideId` is set, return `noChange` without the re-check. Pending promotion still clears the override. Add the missing test: override versus a mid-gap scene holds past `minTrackSec`.\\n80|   If we skip it: the Change track button undoes itself, worst on scenes where the reader's pick scores far below best.\\n81|\\n82|2. **Loop fade restarts on every timeupdate for 3 s** (audible stutter, repeated reloads), `app/player.tsx:86, 145-157`.\\n83|   Problem: `handleTimeUpdate` arms `loopArmedRef` then calls `requestPlayRef`, whose first lines clear `loopArmedRef` back to null. The old element stays `audibleRef` until the fade finishes, so each later timeupdate re-arms, cancels the fade, reassigns `dst.src` (reload), and restarts the fade.\\n84|   Case: any looping track within `crossfadeSec` of its end fires timeupdate about 4 times per second; each one restarts the 3 s loop fade.\\n85|   Fix: delete the unconditional clear at line 86 and clear the arm only on a real track change, e.g. guard it with `trackRef.current?.id !== next.id` before the assignment. One line.\\n86|   If we skip it: every loop point stutters instead of crossfading.\\n87|\\n88|3. **First press can start the same track twice** (self-crossfade), `app/player.tsx:130-141, 174-184`.\\n89|   Problem: first-press `toggle` calls `requestPlay(next, 0)`, then the `[started, trackId]` effect fires on the same track and calls `requestPlay(next, fadeSec)`. When the scheduler already switched pre-press, `fadeSec` can be 3, so the track crossfades into itself on the other element. Even at 0 the `src` is assigned twice.\\n90|   Fix: remove the direct `requestPlay` call from the first-press branch and let the effect do the single start. Note in the diff that a pre-press scheduler switch then gives a 3 s fade-in on first press; force 0 there if Martin wants instant start.\\n91|   If we skip it: readers who read a while before pressing play hear the track restart into itself.\\n92|\\n93|### Should fix\\n94|\\n95|4. **Config override for weights is silently ignored; loop fades bypass the scheduler fade** (one-config rule), `core/music.ts:79-84`, `app/player.tsx:149-168`.\\n96|   Problem: `bhattacharyyaSimilarity` reads `MUSIC_CONFIG.weights` directly, so `rankTracks(scene, m, { weights: custom })` scores with the global weights. Separately, the loop and ended paths hardcode `MUSIC_CONFIG.crossfadeSec` instead of the `fadeSec` prop the scheduler reported, so a custom `crossfadeSec` applies to switches but not loops.\\n97|   Fix: pass `config.weights` into the similarity call in `scoreTrack`/`rankTracks`, and read the loop fade length from `fadeSecRef` instead of the global.\\n98|   If we skip it: tests and future tuning knobs lie about which values are live.\\n99|\\n100|5. **Pause does not freeze the fade** (wrong element resumes), `app/player.tsx:110-127, 185-189`.\\n101|   Problem: pause stops both elements but never cancels or freezes the rAF fade. The tick keeps animating gains and flips `audibleRef` while paused. Resuming mid-fade replays both elements (both levels above 0.02) until the fade converges.\\n102|   Fix: skip the level update while `playingRef` is false and let the scheduled tick continue the fade on resume. Two lines.\\n103|   If we skip it: a pause-resume inside a 3 s fade briefly plays both elements at once.\\n104|\\n105|6. **Ended non-loop track leaves a stale override** (live once finding 1 lands), `core/music-schedule.ts:196-213`.\\n106|   Problem: `noteTrackEnded` correctly updates `currentStartedSec` and excludes the ended id, but keeps the old `overrideId`. Harmless today because nothing reads it; after finding 1 the stale id would wrongly block switches.\\n107|   Fix: clear `overrideId`/`overrideSceneId` in `noteTrackEnded` together with finding 1. The pre-manifest `activeId` versus scheduler divergence (`app/reader.tsx:26, 81-85`) converges on manifest load and needs no change.\\n108|   If we skip it: fixing 1 without this trades one stuck-override bug for another.\\n109|\\n110|### Sequences 1 to 7, verdicts\\n111|\\n112|1. Override overwritten: confirmed. Same scene, gap at or above margin: revert after `minTrackSec` (proven run above); gap at or above `hardCutMargin`: revert within one second. Only the committed fixture's small gaps mask it.\\n113|2. Loop re-trigger: confirmed by reading. The clear at line 86 runs inside every loop-triggered `requestPlay`, so the arm never survives until the fade completes.\\n114|3. First press double start: confirmed, conditional on a scheduler switch before first press setting `fadeSec` to 3 or 1.5. Common case (`fadeSec` 0) still reassigns `src` twice.\\n115|4. Direct `MUSIC_CONFIG.crossfadeSec` in loop/end paths: confirmed for the player loop paths; `noteTrackEnded` correctly uses the resolved config. Weights override dead as described in finding 4.\\n116|5. Pause during fade: confirmed by reading. rAF tick has no `playingRef` gate; pause has no `cancelFade`.\\n117|6. `noteTrackEnded`: updates `currentStartedSec`, ignores the override (finding 6). Reader `activeId` diverges from the scheduler only before the manifest lands and converges through the reselect effect; no fix needed.\\n118|7. Same-emotion Next tests: covered. `core/music.test.ts:116-121` cycle order, wrap, skip current; `:123-126` other-emotion and null current start at top; `:128-140` both fallbacks; `:142-146` null scene id order; `:148-152` one track and none. Scheduler override hold/clear at `core/music-schedule.test.ts:202-218`. Missing only the large-gap override hold (finding 1).\\n119|\\n120|### Checked and fine\\n121|\\n122|- First-review findings 1 to 10 all addressed: observer re-snapshot (`app/reader.tsx:94-98`) with scroll-down, scroll-up, and jump picker tests; pause stops both elements; volume lives in a ref outside the track effect deps; `isVector8` requires finite 0..1 entries; core and picker tests added; contracts names `analysis.json` as the scene source and `scenes.json` as the pipeline intermediate; tie-break by lower id; `SceneSignal` rename; `byId` memo with no flag parameter; reduced-motion listener in state, audio fade always full length. Finding 11 is moot: mid-fade requests cancel and restart from live levels.\\n123|- Manifest v2: version pinned to 2, `title` rename, all required and optional fields with range checks, `startSec` below `durationSec`, `loop` default true, unknown `source` and non-https `sourceUrl` rejected, NaN rejected. Committed manifest parses as v2 with `calma`/`suspenso` hand labels, `generated` source, CC-BY-NC-4.0 license, and MusicGen placeholder attribution.\\n124|- Scheduler: first track immediate, 20 s dwell with newest-pending-wins, 0.07 margin boundary tested both sides, 45 s min-track with 1.5 s hard-cut exception, null scene promotes without switching.\\n125|- Player: no `loop` attribute, `startSec` seek on metadata, non-loop end delegates to the scheduler excluding the ended track, volume never touches `src`, attribution shows composer/artist, license, and source link with `rel=\\\"noopener noreferrer\\\"` and `target _blank`, emotion label shown in Spanish as stored, Change track disabled exactly when `nextTrack` returns null.\\n126|- Core purity holds: no env, `node:`, fetch, or timers in `core/` outside tests. No purple, violet, or gradient in the player or reader.\\n127|- Runs: `npm test` 81/81 across 15 files, `npm run typecheck` clean, `npm run build` clean with `/` prerendered static.\\n128|\\n129|### Not checked\\n130|\\n131|- Audible playback and real scroll behavior were not run. `app/globals.css` and `app/page.tsx` diffs were not reviewed. `npm run test:hooks`, `npm run check:size`, `npm run check:secrets`, and the Modal/Blob paths were not run.\",\"final_result\":true,\"kind\":\"output\",\"task_id\":\"01a18013-6706-7031-a830-dde0960b028c\"},\"kind\":\"task_lifecycle\",\"run_stream\":{\"id\":\"01a18013-60b1-7551-82e2-1b1f3ccd850e\",\"kind\":\"run\"},\"task_id\":\"01a18013-6706-7031-a830-dde0960b028c\",\"task_stream\":{\"id\":\"01a18013-6706-7031-a830-dde0960b028c\",\"kind\":\"task\"}}}\nagent-logs/06-review.jsonl:56:{\"schema_version\":1,\"id\":\"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c3bb\",\"stream\":{\"kind\":\"session\",\"id\":\"01a18013-5db9-7772-9613-fed1b45db42e\"},\"sequence\":56,\"recorded_at\":1780531400000107,\"record_type\":\"event\",\"durability\":\"durable\",\"causation_id\":\"01a18013-60b1-7551-82e2-1b1f3ccd850e\",\"payload_type\":\"tool.result\",\"payload_schema_version\":1,\"payload\":{\"call_id\":\"call_01a1801365d2772985ec7a2e4ab2ad31\",\"command_id\":\"01a18013-60b1-7551-82e2-1b1f3ccd850e\",\"correlation_facts\":{\"outcome\":\"success\",\"tool_name\":\"read_file\"},\"kind\":\"tool_result\",\"run_stream\":{\"id\":\"01a18013-60b1-7551-82e2-1b1f3ccd850e\",\"kind\":\"run\"},\"text\":\"Read text file `docs/reviews/05.md`.\\n1|# Review: task 5 contracts and scene reader\\n2|\\n3|Verdict: fix finding 1 first. The reader renders and plays, but slow scrolling never moves the music to the next scene. Findings 2 to 6 should land in the same pass; 7 to 11 are nits.\\n4|\\n5|What this change does: adds the module contracts in `docs/contracts.md`, pure track selection and manifest parsing in `core/music.ts`, the slim reader model in `core/reader.ts`, a server-only Oz loader in `server/books.ts`, and the client reader (`app/reader.tsx`, `app/active-scene.ts`, `app/player.tsx`) with a two-track placeholder manifest in `public/music/`.\\n6|\\n7|## Findings\\n8|\\n9|1. **Slow scroll down never advances the active scene** (blocker), `app/reader.tsx:107-119`, `app/active-scene.ts:10-25`.\\n10|   Problem: the observer callback scores only the changed entries. A new scene enters the 5 percent band from below with its top under the reading line, so `pickActiveScene` skips it. Its top then crosses the line with no further callback (intersection status does not change), and when the old scene exits, the old entry is filtered out and the result falls back to current. The next scene is adopted only when its top is already above the line at entry, which is the scroll-up direction plus jumps, not scroll-down.\\n11|   Fix: use entries only as a trigger and re-snapshot all sections with live rects on each callback, as the mount path already does. Derive the hit flag from rect versus band in the snapshot mapper.\\n12|\\n13|2. **Pause during a crossfade leaves the incoming element playing** (should-fix), `app/player.tsx:61-80`.\\n14|   Problem: `toggle` pauses only the live element. For 1.5 s after a track change the standby element is the audible one, so pressing pause in that window sets state to paused while audio keeps playing.\\n15|   Fix: pause both refs in `toggle`, or keep the fading pair in one ref both handlers use.\\n16|\\n17|3. **Volume sits in the track-effect deps and restarts fades** (should-fix), `app/player.tsx:28-59`.\\n18|   Problem: every slider tick re-runs the track effect. While paused the early return does not apply (live is paused), so each tick reassigns `standby.src` and flips `liveRef`. Mid-fade it also reassigns the incoming `src`, which reloads that track from zero, and starts a fresh interval.\\n19|   Fix: drop `volume` from the deps, read it through a ref inside the fade, and return early when the live element already carries the track `src` regardless of paused state.\\n20|\\n21|4. **Validator accepts NaN vector entries** (should-fix), `core/music.ts:34-37`.\\n22|   Problem: `isVector8` checks `typeof` only, and `typeof NaN` is `number`. A NaN entry passes `parseManifest`, then poisons the cosine score and the sort order for that track.\\n23|   Fix: require `Number.isFinite` for each of the 8 values, one word in the same check.\\n24|\\n25|5. **Tests skip the behaviors the brief asked about** (should-fix), `core/music.test.ts`, `app/reader.tsx:36-61`.\\n26|   Problem: no test covers `nextAlternative` with a null scene, `selectTrack` with an excluded current track, the skip override held until the scene change and then used as current, or reselection when the manifest lands after the first scene. The observer wiring has no test beyond the pure picker.\\n27|   Fix: add the three core cases (null scene alternative, excluded current, excluded all) and pull `applyScene` into a pure helper beside `active-scene.ts` with two tests: override as base on scene change, cleared after.\\n28|\\n29|6. **Doc says the reader consumes `scenes.json`, code never reads it** (should-fix), `docs/contracts.md:11-20`, `server/books.ts:9-17`.\\n30|   Problem: `loadOzBook` reads `book.json` plus `analysis.json` only, which is fine because analysis carries every scene field, but the contract lists `scenes.json` as an input the reader consumes.\\n31|   Fix: name `analysis.json` as the scene source and `scenes.json` as the pipeline intermediate it mirrors, in one sentence.\\n32|\\n33|7. **Tie-break repeats an index scan per comparison** (nit), `core/music.ts:96-99`.\\n34|   Problem: the comparator calls `manifest.tracks.indexOf` on each tie. Sort is already stable, so ties follow manifest order without it.\\n35|   Fix: delete the tie branch and return the diff.\\n36|\\n37|8. **Two `SceneEmotion` types with different shapes** (nit), `core/music.ts:22-26`, `core/types.ts:78-83`.\\n38|   Problem: `core/music.ts` exports `SceneEmotion` as `{ vector, intensity, tempo }` while `core/types.ts` uses the same name for `{ jev, muse_override, final, error }`. Each reads fine alone; importing both invites the wrong one.\\n39|   Fix: rename the music one to `SceneSignal` or reuse an inline param type.\\n40|\\n41|9. **Snapshot helper takes a flag it never varies** (nit), `app/reader.tsx:31, 101-106`.\\n42|   Problem: `snapshot(hit)` is called once with `true`, and `byId.current` is rebuilt on every render.\\n43|   Fix: delete the parameter and build the map with `useMemo` on `scenes`.\\n44|\\n45|10. **Reduced-motion choice never updates** (nit), `app/player.tsx:26`.\\n46|    Problem: `matchMedia` runs per render with no listener, so flipping the OS setting mid session keeps the old fade until a rerender for another reason.\\n47|    Fix: read it once in state with a change listener, or leave it; the wrongness lasts one session at most.\\n48|\\n49|11. **Track swap mid-fade restarts from partial volumes** (nit), `app/player.tsx:43-56`.\\n50|    Problem: the cleanup clears the old interval but leaves the old live element at partial volume, and the new run fades from there while the incoming `src` is replaced. Playback converges, only the fade curve kinks.\\n51|    Fix: nothing required once finding 3 lands; note it only if the effect is reworked anyway.\\n52|\\n53|## Checked and fine\\n54|\\n55|- Core purity: no `process.env`, `node:` imports, `fetch`, or `fs` in `core/` outside tests. Import direction holds: `app/page.tsx` imports `server/books.ts`, client files import only `core/` and siblings, `server/books.ts` starts with `import 'server-only'`.\\n56|- Client payload: only scene ids, titles, and emotion triples pass to `Reader`. `buildReaderModel` spreads `final` (`vector`, `intensity`, `tempo`) and drops `jev`, `muse_override`, provenance. The reader test asserts both internals are absent.\\n57|- Image and chat types match the spec: `{ bookId, textVersion, firstN, lastN }` to `{ url }`, and `{ bookId, textVersion, positionN, spoilerMode, messages }` with `{ role, text }` messages. Contract only, no routes.\\n58|- Manifest trust boundary: the client parses every fetch with `parseManifest`, which rejects unknown versions, missing fields, short vectors, out-of-range numbers, and non-`/music/` non-https `src`. Bad drop-ins fail loudly.\\n59|- CSP unchanged and sufficient: `media-src 'self' blob:` covers the placeholder clips, `connect-src 'self'` covers the manifest fetch. Both docs note remote https tracks need a `media-src` edit.\\n60|- Reading line consistent with the band: the band spans 30 to 35 percent of viewport height, the line sits at one third, inside the band. Short scenes still cross it because sections span their paragraphs.\\n61|- Swap guide: `public/music/README.md` replaces files plus manifest plus version bump, names `parseManifest` as the shape check, and carries the CC-BY-NC non-commercial note. Swap needs no code change.\\n62|- Design: styles use tokens only (all names exist in `app/tokens.css`), accent is Meta blue on borders and focus, no purple or gradients, controls are real buttons and inputs with labels and visible focus, no UI transition over 200 ms (audio fade is not UI motion).\\n63|- Prose: `docs/contracts.md` and the README are short, sentence case, no filler or banned words.\\n64|- Runs: `npm test` 63/63 across 14 files, `npm run typecheck` clean, `npm run build` clean with `/` prerendered static.\\n65|\\n66|## Not checked\\n67|\\n68|- Audible playback, real scroll behavior, and screen-reader pass were not run; the observer finding rests on reading plus band math, not a browser session. Live manifest fetch against the built server was not repeated.\\n69|\\n70|## Round 2\\n71|\\n72|What this change does: the fix pass answers findings 1 to 10, adds manifest v2 with hand-labeled emotions, a pure scheduler with dwell/hysteresis/min-track/hard-cut, same-emotion Next, and a two-element player rewrite with loop crossfades and attribution. The rules all land. Three player/scheduler defects do not.\\n73|\\n74|### Must fix\\n75|\\n76|1. **Reader skip choice reverts on the same scene** (breaks Martin's rule), `core/music-schedule.ts:60-100, 151-166`.\\n77|   Problem: `evaluateSwitch` never reads `overrideId`, and `tickScheduler` re-runs it every second. After Change track the override is a dead field: it is set in `requestNext` (`music-schedule.ts:185-186`) and cleared in `promote`, but nothing checks it.\\n78|   Case (run against the real scheduler): scene pure tristeza, tracks pure/bland tristeza plus calm; Next moves pure to bland with gap 0.145, then `tickScheduler` at 45 s after the press switches back to pure on the same scene, stale `overrideId: bland` still set. Gaps at or above `hardCutMargin` revert within one second instead. The committed fixture hides this only because its same-emotion gaps sit below `switchMargin`.\\n79|   Fix: in `tickScheduler`, when there is no pending scene and `overrideId` is set, return `noChange` without the re-check. Pending promotion still clears the override. Add the missing test: override versus a mid-gap scene holds past `minTrackSec`.\\n80|   If we skip it: the Change track button undoes itself, worst on scenes where the reader's pick scores far below best.\\n81|\\n82|2. **Loop fade restarts on every timeupdate for 3 s** (audible stutter, repeated reloads), `app/player.tsx:86, 145-157`.\\n83|   Problem: `handleTimeUpdate` arms `loopArmedRef` then calls `requestPlayRef`, whose first lines clear `loopArmedRef` back to null. The old element stays `audibleRef` until the fade finishes, so each later timeupdate re-arms, cancels the fade, reassigns `dst.src` (reload), and restarts the fade.\\n84|   Case: any looping track within `crossfadeSec` of its end fires timeupdate about 4 times per second; each one restarts the 3 s loop fade.\\n85|   Fix: delete the unconditional clear at line 86 and clear the arm only on a real track change, e.g. guard it with `trackRef.current?.id !== next.id` before the assignment. One line.\\n86|   If we skip it: every loop point stutters instead of crossfading.\\n87|\\n88|3. **First press can start the same track twice** (self-crossfade), `app/player.tsx:130-141, 174-184`.\\n89|   Problem: first-press `toggle` calls `requestPlay(next, 0)`, then the `[started, trackId]` effect fires on the same track and calls `requestPlay(next, fadeSec)`. When the scheduler already switched pre-press, `fadeSec` can be 3, so the track crossfades into itself on the other element. Even at 0 the `src` is assigned twice.\\n90|   Fix: remove the direct `requestPlay` call from the first-press branch and let the effect do the single start. Note in the diff that a pre-press scheduler switch then gives a 3 s fade-in on first press; force 0 there if Martin wants instant start.\\n91|   If we skip it: readers who read a while before pressing play hear the track restart into itself.\\n92|\\n93|### Should fix\\n94|\\n95|4. **Config override for weights is silently ignored; loop fades bypass the scheduler fade** (one-config rule), `core/music.ts:79-84`, `app/player.tsx:149-168`.\\n96|   Problem: `bhattacharyyaSimilarity` reads `MUSIC_CONFIG.weights` directly, so `rankTracks(scene, m, { weights: custom })` scores with the global weights. Separately, the loop and ended paths hardcode `MUSIC_CONFIG.crossfadeSec` instead of the `fadeSec` prop the scheduler reported, so a custom `crossfadeSec` applies to switches but not loops.\\n97|   Fix: pass `config.weights` into the similarity call in `scoreTrack`/`rankTracks`, and read the loop fade length from `fadeSecRef` instead of the global.\\n98|   If we skip it: tests and future tuning knobs lie about which values are live.\\n99|\\n100|5. **Pause does not freeze the fade** (wrong element resumes), `app/player.tsx:110-127, 185-189`.\\n101|   Problem: pause stops both elements but never cancels or freezes the rAF fade. The tick keeps animating gains and flips `audibleRef` while paused. Resuming mid-fade replays both elements (both levels above 0.02) until the fade converges.\\n102|   Fix: skip the level update while `playingRef` is false and let the scheduled tick continue the fade on resume. Two lines.\\n103|   If we skip it: a pause-resume inside a 3 s fade briefly plays both elements at once.\\n104|\\n105|6. **Ended non-loop track leaves a stale override** (live once finding 1 lands), `core/music-schedule.ts:196-213`.\\n106|   Problem: `noteTrackEnded` correctly updates `currentStartedSec` and excludes the ended id, but keeps the old `overrideId`. Harmless today because nothing reads it; after finding 1 the stale id would wrongly block switches.\\n107|   Fix: clear `overrideId`/`overrideSceneId` in `noteTrackEnded` together with finding 1. The pre-manifest `activeId` versus scheduler divergence (`app/reader.tsx:26, 81-85`) converges on manifest load and needs no change.\\n108|   If we skip it: fixing 1 without this trades one stuck-override bug for another.\\n109|\\n110|### Sequences 1 to 7, verdicts\\n111|\\n112|1. Override overwritten: confirmed. Same scene, gap at or above margin: revert after `minTrackSec` (proven run above); gap at or above `hardCutMargin`: revert within one second. Only the committed fixture's small gaps mask it.\\n113|2. Loop re-trigger: confirmed by reading. The clear at line 86 runs inside every loop-triggered `requestPlay`, so the arm never survives until the fade completes.\\n114|3. First press double start: confirmed, conditional on a scheduler switch before first press setting `fadeSec` to 3 or 1.5. Common case (`fadeSec` 0) still reassigns `src` twice.\\n115|4. Direct `MUSIC_CONFIG.crossfadeSec` in loop/end paths: confirmed for the player loop paths; `noteTrackEnded` correctly uses the resolved config. Weights override dead as described in finding 4.\\n116|5. Pause during fade: confirmed by reading. rAF tick has no `playingRef` gate; pause has no `cancelFade`.\\n117|6. `noteTrackEnded`: updates `currentStartedSec`, ignores the override (finding 6). Reader `activeId` diverges from the scheduler only before the manifest lands and converges through the reselect effect; no fix needed.\\n118|7. Same-emotion Next tests: covered. `core/music.test.ts:116-121` cycle order, wrap, skip current; `:123-126` other-emotion and null current start at top; `:128-140` both fallbacks; `:142-146` null scene id order; `:148-152` one track and none. Scheduler override hold/clear at `core/music-schedule.test.ts:202-218`. Missing only the large-gap override hold (finding 1).\\n119|\\n120|### Checked and fine\\n121|\\n122|- First-review findings 1 to 10 all addressed: observer re-snapshot (`app/reader.tsx:94-98`) with scroll-down, scroll-up, and jump picker tests; pause stops both elements; volume lives in a ref outside the track effect deps; `isVector8` requires finite 0..1 entries; core and picker tests added; contracts names `analysis.json` as the scene source and `scenes.json` as the pipeline intermediate; tie-break by lower id; `SceneSignal` rename; `byId` memo with no flag parameter; reduced-motion listener in state, audio fade always full length. Finding 11 is moot: mid-fade requests cancel and restart from live levels.\\n123|- Manifest v2: version pinned to 2, `title` rename, all required and optional fields with range checks, `startSec` below `durationSec`, `loop` default true, unknown `source` and non-https `sourceUrl` rejected, NaN rejected. Committed manifest parses as v2 with `calma`/`suspenso` hand labels, `generated` source, CC-BY-NC-4.0 license, and MusicGen placeholder attribution.\\n124|- Scheduler: first track immediate, 20 s dwell with newest-pending-wins, 0.07 margin boundary tested both sides, 45 s min-track with 1.5 s hard-cut exception, null scene promotes without switching.\\n125|- Player: no `loop` attribute, `startSec` seek on metadata, non-loop end delegates to the scheduler excluding the ended track, volume never touches `src`, attribution shows composer/artist, license, and source link with `rel=\\\"noopener noreferrer\\\"` and `target _blank`, emotion label shown in Spanish as stored, Change track disabled exactly when `nextTrack` returns null.\\n126|- Core purity holds: no env, `node:`, fetch, or timers in `core/` outside tests. No purple, violet, or gradient in the player or reader.\\n127|- Runs: `npm test` 81/81 across 15 files, `npm run typecheck` clean, `npm run build` clean with `/` prerendered static.\\n128|\\n129|### Not checked\\n130|\\n131|- Audible playback and real scroll behavior were not run. `app/globals.css` and `app/page.tsx` diffs were not reviewed. `npm run test:hooks`, `npm run check:size`, `npm run check:secrets`, and the Modal/Blob paths were not run.\"}}\nagent-logs/06-review.jsonl:208:{\"schema_version\":1,\"id\":\"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c4eb\",\"stream\":{\"kind\":\"session\",\"id\":\"01a18013-5db9-7772-9613-fed1b45db42e\"},\"sequence\":208,\"recorded_at\":1780531400000411,\"record_type\":\"event\",\"durability\":\"durable\",\"causation_id\":\"01a18013-60b1-7551-82e2-1b1f3ccd850e\",\"payload_type\":\"task.lifecycle.output\",\"payload_schema_version\":1,\"payload\":{\"command_id\":\"01a18013-60b1-7551-82e2-1b1f3ccd850e\",\"event\":{\"chunk\":\"Read text file `core/music.ts`.\\n1|// Track selection and manifest parsing. Pure: no env, no fetch, no audio.\\n2|import { EMOTIONS } from \\\"./types\\\";\\n3|import type { EmotionId, Vector8 } from \\\"./types\\\";\\n4|import { buildFeatures } from \\\"./cluster\\\";\\n5|\\n6|// Hand label for the track: the single emotion it was made to carry.\\n7|export type TrackSource = \\\"generated\\\" | \\\"jamendo\\\" | \\\"recording\\\";\\n8|\\n9|export interface Playlist {\\n10|  id: string;\\n11|  label: string;\\n12|  trackIds: string[];\\n13|}\\n14|\\n15|// Fixed id for the owner-requested Chopin playlist. The player button\\n16|// uses the playlist with this id and shows its label verbatim.\\n17|export const CHOPIN_PLAYLIST_ID = \\\"just-play-chopin\\\";\\n18|\\n19|export interface Track {\\n20|  id: string;\\n21|  src: string;\\n22|  title: string;\\n23|  playlistOnly?: boolean;\\n24|  emotion: EmotionId;\\n25|  vector: Vector8;\\n26|  intensity: number;\\n27|  tempo: number;\\n28|  durationSec: number;\\n29|  startSec: number;\\n30|  loop: boolean;\\n31|  soundtrack: string;\\n32|  style: string;\\n33|  source?: TrackSource;\\n34|  artist?: string;\\n35|  composer?: string;\\n36|  license?: string;\\n37|  attribution?: string;\\n38|  sourceUrl?: string;\\n39|}\\n40|\\n41|export interface StyleInfo {\\n42|  id: string;\\n43|  name: string;\\n44|}\\n45|\\n46|export interface Soundtrack {\\n47|  id: string;\\n48|  name: string;\\n49|  style: string;\\n50|  credit?: string;\\n51|}\\n52|\\n53|export interface MusicManifest {\\n54|  version: number;\\n55|  styles: StyleInfo[];\\n56|  soundtracks: Soundtrack[];\\n57|  tracks: Track[];\\n58|  playlists: Playlist[];\\n59|}\\n60|\\n61|// Session selection: style scopes every pick, soundtrackId is the home\\n62|// in soundtrack mode, mode picks the ranking rule.\\n63|export interface MusicSelection {\\n64|  mode: \\\"soundtrack\\\" | \\\"random\\\";\\n65|  soundtrackId: string | null;\\n66|  style: string | null;\\n67|}\\n68|\\n69|export type Rng = () => number;\\n70|\\n71|export interface SelectEnv {\\n72|  selection: MusicSelection;\\n73|  rng: Rng;\\n74|}\\n75|\\n76|export interface PersistedMusicPrefs {\\n77|  mode: \\\"soundtrack\\\" | \\\"random\\\";\\n78|  soundtrackId: string | null;\\n79|  style: string | null;\\n80|}\\n81|\\n82|export interface SceneSignal {\\n83|  vector: Vector8;\\n84|  intensity: number;\\n85|  tempo: number;\\n86|}\\n87|\\n88|export type Similarity = (scene: SceneSignal, track: Track, weights: MusicWeights) => number;\\n89|\\n90|export interface MusicWeights {\\n91|  emotion: number;\\n92|  intensity: number;\\n93|  tempo: number;\\n94|}\\n95|\\n96|export interface MusicConfig {\\n97|  similarity: Similarity;\\n98|  weights: MusicWeights;\\n99|  switchMargin: number;\\n100|  dwellSec: number;\\n101|  minTrackSec: number;\\n102|  hardCutMargin: number;\\n103|  crossfadeSec: number;\\n104|  hardCutCrossfadeSec: number;\\n105|  randomTolerance: number;\\n106|}\\n107|\\n108|// Renormalize the 8 entries to sum 1. Extra keys (such as a Jev\\n109|// \\\"unknown\\\" entry) are ignored. An all-zero vector stays all zero.\\n110|export function normalize8(vector: Record<string, number>): number[] {\\n111|  const values = EMOTIONS.map((id: EmotionId) => {\\n112|    const v = vector[id];\\n113|    return typeof v === \\\"number\\\" && Number.isFinite(v) ? v : 0;\\n114|  });\\n115|  const sum = values.reduce((a, b) => a + b, 0);\\n116|  if (sum <= 0) return values.map(() => 0);\\n117|  return values.map((v) => v / sum);\\n118|}\\n119|\\n120|// Bhattacharyya affinity over the renormalized shapes, plus separate\\n121|// intensity and tempo terms. Fair to blended scenes, unlike cosine.\\n122|export function bhattacharyyaSimilarity(\\n123|  scene: SceneSignal,\\n124|  track: Track,\\n125|  weights: MusicWeights = MUSIC_CONFIG.weights,\\n126|): number {\\n127|  const s = normalize8(scene.vector);\\n128|  const t = normalize8(track.vector);\\n129|  let affinity = 0;\\n130|  for (let i = 0; i < s.length; i++) {\\n131|    affinity += Math.sqrt((s[i] ?? 0) * (t[i] ?? 0));\\n132|  }\\n133|  return (\\n134|    weights.emotion * affinity +\\n135|    weights.intensity * (1 - Math.abs(scene.intensity - track.intensity)) +\\n136|    weights.tempo * (1 - Math.abs(scene.tempo - track.tempo))\\n137|  );\\n138|}\\n139|\\n140|// Cosine over buildFeatures output (vector plus weighted intensity and\\n141|// tempo). Kept as an alternative; it favors peaky scenes.\\n142|export function cosineSimilarity(scene: SceneSignal, track: Track): number {\\n143|  const a = buildFeatures(scene);\\n144|  const b = buildFeatures(track);\\n145|  let dot = 0;\\n146|  let na = 0;\\n147|  let nb = 0;\\n148|  for (let i = 0; i < a.length; i++) {\\n149|    const x = a[i] ?? 0;\\n150|    const y = b[i] ?? 0;\\n151|    dot += x * y;\\n152|    na += x * x;\\n153|    nb += y * y;\\n154|  }\\n155|  if (na === 0 || nb === 0) return 0;\\n156|  return dot / (Math.sqrt(na) * Math.sqrt(nb));\\n157|}\\n158|\\n159|export const MUSIC_CONFIG: MusicConfig = {\\n160|  similarity: bhattacharyyaSimilarity,\\n161|  weights: { emotion: 0.7, intensity: 0.15, tempo: 0.15 },\\n162|  switchMargin: 0.07,\\n163|  dwellSec: 20,\\n164|  minTrackSec: 45,\\n165|  hardCutMargin: 0.2,\\n166|  crossfadeSec: 3,\\n167|  hardCutCrossfadeSec: 1.5,\\n168|  // Admits near ties into the random-mode draw without letting clearly\\n169|  // worse matches in.\\n170|  randomTolerance: 0.05,\\n171|};\\n172|\\n173|export function resolveConfig(override?: Partial<MusicConfig>): MusicConfig {\\n174|  if (!override) return MUSIC_CONFIG;\\n175|  return {\\n176|    ...MUSIC_CONFIG,\\n177|    ...override,\\n178|    weights: override.weights ?? MUSIC_CONFIG.weights,\\n179|  };\\n180|}\\n181|\\n182|export function scoreTrack(\\n183|  scene: SceneSignal,\\n184|  track: Track,\\n185|  override?: Partial<MusicConfig>,\\n186|): number {\\n187|  const config = resolveConfig(override);\\n188|  return config.similarity(scene, track, config.weights);\\n189|}\\n190|\\n191|// Best score first. Ties go to the lower track id, so ranking is stable.\\n192|export function rankTracks(\\n193|  scene: SceneSignal,\\n194|  manifest: MusicManifest,\\n195|  override?: Partial<MusicConfig>,\\n196|): Track[] {\\n197|  const config = resolveConfig(override);\\n198|  return [...manifest.tracks].sort((a, b) => {\\n199|    const diff =\\n200|      config.similarity(scene, b, config.weights) - config.similarity(scene, a, config.weights);\\n201|    if (diff !== 0) return diff;\\n202|    return a.id < b.id ? -1 : a.id > b.id ? 1 : 0;\\n203|  });\\n204|}\\n205|\\n206|// Dominant emotion of a scene: argmax of the renormalized vector, with\\n207|// ties broken by EMOTIONS order.\\n208|export function dominantEmotion(scene: SceneSignal): EmotionId {\\n209|  const norm = normalize8(scene.vector);\\n210|  let best: EmotionId = EMOTIONS[0] as EmotionId;\\n211|  let bestValue = -Infinity;\\n212|  EMOTIONS.forEach((id: EmotionId, i: number) => {\\n213|    const value = norm[i] ?? 0;\\n214|    if (value > bestValue) {\\n215|      bestValue = value;\\n216|      best = id;\\n217|    }\\n218|  });\\n219|  return best;\\n220|}\\n221|\\n222|// Reader skip rule: cycle tracks hand-labeled with the scene's dominant\\n223|// emotion, in score order, wrapping and skipping the current track. When\\n224|// the current track has another emotion, start at the top candidate. With\\n225|// no other same-emotion track, fall back to the best track overall that\\n226|// Style scope for every pick. A null style means the whole manifest,\\n227|// which only happens before the reader resolves the session style.\\n228|// Style scope for every pick, minus playlist-only tracks. Playlist tracks\\n229|// never enter emotion selection, so the filter lives here, not in callers.\\n230|export function candidatesFor(selection: MusicSelection, manifest: MusicManifest): Track[] {\\n231|  const audible = manifest.tracks.filter((t) => t.playlistOnly !== true);\\n232|  if (selection.style === null) return audible;\\n233|  return audible.filter((t) => t.style === selection.style);\\n234|}\\n235|\\n236|// Home set in soundtrack mode: the session soundtrack, or the whole\\n237|// style set when none is set yet.\\n238|export function homeTracks(selection: MusicSelection, styleTracks: Track[]): Track[] {\\n239|  if (selection.soundtrackId === null) return styleTracks;\\n240|  const home = styleTracks.filter((t) => t.soundtrack === selection.soundtrackId);\\n241|  return home.length > 0 ? home : styleTracks;\\n242|}\\n243|\\n244|// \\\"Cambiar track\\\": the next same-emotion track in score order, wrapping\\n245|// and skipping the current. In soundtrack mode it stays inside the\\n246|// current track's soundtrack first, then tries the same emotion in other\\n247|// same-style soundtracks, then the best same-style track overall. In\\n248|// random mode it ranges over all same-style soundtracks at once. A null\\n249|// scene cycles the style set in id order. One track or none gives null.\\n250|export function nextTrack(\\n251|  scene: SceneSignal | null,\\n252|  manifest: MusicManifest,\\n253|  currentTrackId: string | null,\\n254|  override?: Partial<MusicConfig>,\\n255|  selection?: MusicSelection | null,\\n256|): Track | null {\\n257|  const scope =\\n258|    selection == null\\n259|      ? manifest.tracks.filter((t) => t.playlistOnly !== true)\\n260|      : candidatesFor(selection, manifest);\\n261|  if (scope.length <= 1) return null;\\n262|  const config = resolveConfig(override);\\n263|  const scoped = { ...manifest, tracks: scope };\\n264|  if (scene === null) {\\n265|    const ids = [...scope].sort((a, b) => (a.id < b.id ? -1 : a.id > b.id ? 1 : 0));\\n266|    const at = ids.findIndex((t) => t.id === currentTrackId);\\n267|    return ids[(at + 1) % ids.length] as Track;\\n268|  }\\n269|  const ranked = rankTracks(scene, scoped, config);\\n270|  const same = ranked.filter((t) => t.emotion === dominantEmotion(scene));\\n271|  const others = same.filter((t) => t.id !== currentTrackId);\\n272|  if (others.length > 0) {\\n273|    if (selection?.mode === \\\"random\\\") {\\n274|      const at = same.findIndex((t) => t.id === currentTrackId);\\n275|      if (at >= 0) return same[(at + 1) % same.length] as Track;\\n276|      return same[0] as Track;\\n277|    }\\n278|    const current = scope.find((t) => t.id === currentTrackId) ?? null;\\n279|    const home = current ? same.filter((t) => t.soundtrack === current.soundtrack) : [];\\n280|    const homeOthers = home.filter((t) => t.id !== currentTrackId);\\n281|    if (homeOthers.length > 0) {\\n282|      const at = home.findIndex((t) => t.id === currentTrackId);\\n283|      if (at >= 0) return home[(at + 1) % home.length] as Track;\\n284|      return home[0] as Track;\\n285|    }\\n286|    const at = same.findIndex((t) => t.id === currentTrackId);\\n287|    if (at >= 0) return same[(at + 1) % same.length] as Track;\\n288|    return same[0] as Track;\\n289|  }\\n290|  return ranked.find((t) => t.id !== currentTrackId) ?? null;\\n291|}\\n292|\\n293|// Random mode draw: same-style tracks with the scene's dominant emotion\\n294|// (or the whole style set when none matches), scored, kept within\\n295|// randomTolerance of the best. The current track stays when eligible;\\n296|// otherwise the draw skips it when an alternative exists.\\n297|export function pickRandomTrack(\\n298|  cands: Track[],\\n299|  scene: SceneSignal | null,\\n300|  excludeId: string | null,\\n301|  rng: Rng,\\n302|  override?: Partial<MusicConfig>,\\n303|): Track | null {\\n304|  if (cands.length === 0) return null;\\n305|  if (scene === null) {\\n306|    const ids = [...cands].sort((a, b) => (a.id < b.id ? -1 : a.id > b.id ? 1 : 0));\\n307|    const at = ids.findIndex((t) => t.id === excludeId);\\n308|    return ids[(at + 1) % ids.length] as Track;\\n309|  }\\n310|  const config = resolveConfig(override);\\n311|  const scoped = { version: 3, styles: [], soundtracks: [], playlists: [], tracks: cands };\\n312|  const ranked = rankTracks(scene, scoped, config);\\n313|  const dom = dominantEmotion(scene);\\n314|  const pool = ranked.filter((t) => t.emotion === dom);\\n315|  const kept = (pool.length > 0 ? pool : ranked).map((t) => ({\\n316|    track: t,\\n317|    score: config.similarity(scene, t, config.weights),\\n318|  }));\\n319|  const best = kept[0]?.score ?? 0;\\n320|  const eligible = kept.filter((e) => e.score >= best - config.randomTolerance);\\n321|  const current = excludeId !== null ? eligible.find((e) => e.track.id === excludeId) : undefined;\\n322|  if (current) return current.track;\\n323|  const rest = eligible.filter((e) => e.track.id !== excludeId);\\n324|  const drawFrom = rest.length > 0 ? rest : eligible;\\n325|  if (drawFrom.length === 0) return null;\\n326|  return (drawFrom[Math.floor(rng() * drawFrom.length)] as { track: Track }).track;\\n327|}\\n328|\\n329|// Distinct hand-labeled emotions on a soundtrack, ignoring playlist-only\\n330|// tracks. The initial session soundtrack is the one covering most\\n331|// emotions, ties by lower id.\\n332|export function soundtrackCoverage(manifest: MusicManifest, soundtrackId: string): number {\\n333|  return new Set(\\n334|    manifest.tracks\\n335|      .filter((t) => t.soundtrack === soundtrackId && t.playlistOnly !== true)\\n336|      .map((t) => t.emotion),\\n337|  ).size;\\n338|}\\n339|\\n340|export function pickInitialSoundtrack(\\n341|  manifest: MusicManifest,\\n342|  persistedId: string | null,\\n343|): string | null {\\n344|  if (persistedId !== null && manifest.soundtracks.some((s) => s.id === persistedId)) {\\n345|    return persistedId;\\n346|  }\\n347|  let best: string | null = null;\\n348|  let bestCover = -1;\\n349|  for (const s of manifest.soundtracks) {\\n350|    if (!manifest.tracks.some((t) => t.soundtrack === s.id && t.playlistOnly !== true)) continue;\\n351|    const cover = soundtrackCoverage(manifest, s.id);\\n352|    if (cover > bestCover || (cover === bestCover && (best === null || s.id < best))) {\\n353|      best = s.id;\\n354|      bestCover = cover;\\n355|    }\\n356|  }\\n357|  return best;\\n358|}\\n359|\\n360|// True when the style has at least one emotion-selectable track. The style\\n361|// selector uses this, so a style with only playlist tracks stays hidden.\\n362|export function styleHasTracks(manifest: MusicManifest, style: string): boolean {\\n363|  return manifest.tracks.some((t) => t.style === style && t.playlistOnly !== true);\\n364|}\\n365|\\n366|// Session defaults on load. A stored style with no tracks and a stored\\n367|// soundtrack outside the stored style both fall back to the defaults.\\n368|export function resolveInitialSelection(\\n369|  manifest: MusicManifest,\\n370|  persisted: PersistedMusicPrefs | null,\\n371|): MusicSelection {\\n372|  const fallbackId = pickInitialSoundtrack(manifest, null);\\n373|  const fallbackStyle =\\n374|    fallbackId !== null\\n375|      ? (manifest.soundtracks.find((s) => s.id === fallbackId)?.style ?? null)\\n376|      : null;\\n377|  const style =\\n378|    persisted?.style !== null &&\\n379|    persisted?.style !== undefined &&\\n380|    styleHasTracks(manifest, persisted.style)\\n381|      ? persisted.style\\n382|      : fallbackStyle;\\n383|  let soundtrackId: string | null = null;\\n384|  if (style !== null) {\\n385|    const inStyle = (id: string) =>\\n386|      manifest.soundtracks.some((s) => s.id === id && s.style === style);\\n387|    if (\\n388|      persisted?.soundtrackId !== null &&\\n389|      persisted?.soundtrackId !== undefined &&\\n390|      inStyle(persisted.soundtrackId)\\n391|    ) {\\n392|      soundtrackId = persisted.soundtrackId;\\n393|    } else {\\n394|      let best: string | null = null;\\n395|      let bestCover = -1;\\n396|      for (const s of manifest.soundtracks.filter((s) => s.style === style)) {\\n397|        if (!manifest.tracks.some((t) => t.soundtrack === s.id && t.playlistOnly !== true)) {\\n398|          continue;\\n399|        }\\n400|        const cover = soundtrackCoverage(manifest, s.id);\\n401|        if (cover > bestCover || (cover === bestCover && (best === null || s.id < best))) {\\n402|          best = s.id;\\n403|          bestCover = cover;\\n404|        }\\n405|      }\\n406|      soundtrackId = best;\\n407|    }\\n408|  }\\n409|  return {\\n410|    mode: persisted?.mode === \\\"random\\\" ? \\\"random\\\" : \\\"soundtrack\\\",\\n411|    soundtrackId,\\n412|    style,\\n413|  };\\n414|}\\n415|\\n416|// Style change from user action: the session soundtrack becomes the best\\n417|// coverage soundtrack in the new style, and the track is the best match\\n418|// for the scene within the new style. Never crosses styles. Null when\\n419|// the style has no tracks.\\n420|export function requestStyleChange(\\n421|  manifest: MusicManifest,\\n422|  style: string,\\n423|  scene: SceneSignal | null,\\n424|  override?: Partial<MusicConfig>,\\n425|): { soundtrackId: string; track: Track } | null {\\n426|  const scoped = manifest.tracks.filter((t) => t.style === style && t.playlistOnly !== true);\\n427|  if (scoped.length === 0) return null;\\n428|  const config = resolveConfig(override);\\n429|  const inStyle = manifest.soundtracks.filter(\\n430|    (s) => s.style === style && scoped.some((t) => t.soundtrack === s.id),\\n431|  );\\n432|  let soundtrackId = inStyle[0]?.id ?? scoped[0]?.soundtrack ?? \\\"\\\";\\n433|  let bestCover = -1;\\n434|  for (const s of inStyle) {\\n435|    const cover = soundtrackCoverage(manifest, s.id);\\n436|    if (cover > bestCover || (cover === bestCover && s.id < soundtrackId)) {\\n437|      soundtrackId = s.id;\\n438|      bestCover = cover;\\n439|    }\\n440|  }\\n441|  const scopedManifest = { ...manifest, tracks: scoped };\\n442|  let track: Track;\\n443|  if (scene === null) {\\n444|    track = [...scoped].sort((a, b) => (a.id < b.id ? -1 : a.id > b.id ? 1 : 0))[0] as Track;\\n445|  } else {\\n446|    track = rankTracks(scene, scopedManifest, config)[0] as Track;\\n447|  }\\n448|  return { soundtrackId, track };\\n449|}\\n450|\\n451|const SUPPORTED_VERSION = 3;\\n452|const SOURCES = [\\\"generated\\\", \\\"jamendo\\\", \\\"recording\\\"] as const;\\n453|const SLUG = /^[a-z0-9-]+$/;\\n454|\\n455|function isRecord(value: unknown): value is Record<string, unknown> {\\n456|  return typeof value === \\\"object\\\" && value !== null && !Array.isArray(value);\\n457|}\\n458|\\n459|function isOneOf<T extends string>(value: unknown, allowed: readonly T[]): value is T {\\n460|  return typeof value === \\\"string\\\" && allowed.some((entry) => entry === value);\\n461|}\\n462|\\n463|function isVector8(value: unknown): value is Vector8 {\\n464|  if (!isRecord(value)) return false;\\n465|  return EMOTIONS.every(\\n466|    (id: EmotionId) =>\\n467|      typeof value[id] === \\\"number\\\" &&\\n468|      Number.isFinite(value[id]) &&\\n469|      (value[id] as number) >= 0 &&\\n470|      (value[id] as number) <= 1,\\n471|  );\\n472|}\\n473|\\n474|function isUnit(value: unknown): value is number {\\n475|  return typeof value === \\\"number\\\" && Number.isFinite(value) && value >= 0 && value <= 1;\\n476|}\\n477|\\n478|function isSrc(value: unknown): value is string {\\n479|  return (\\n480|    typeof value === \\\"string\\\" && (value.startsWith(\\\"/music/\\\") || value.startsWith(\\\"https://\\\"))\\n481|  );\\n482|}\\n483|\\n484|function isNonEmptyString(value: unknown): value is string {\\n485|  return typeof value === \\\"string\\\" && value !== \\\"\\\";\\n486|}\\n487|\\n488|// Fail loudly on a bad drop-in manifest so broken files never play quiet.\\n489|export function parseManifest(json: unknown): MusicManifest {\\n490|  if (!isRecord(json)) throw new Error(\\\"manifest must be an object\\\");\\n491|  if (json.version !== 3 && json.version !== 2) {\\n492|    throw new Error(`unsupported manifest version: ${String(json.version)}`);\\n493|  }\\n494|  // A v2 manifest becomes one implicit soundtrack holding every track.\\n495|  if (json.version === 2) {\\n496|    if (!Array.isArray(json.tracks)) throw new Error(\\\"manifest tracks must be an array\\\");\\n497|    const tracks = json.tracks.map((entry, i) => parseTrack(entry, i, \\\"default\\\", \\\"orchestral\\\"));\\n498|    return {\\n499|      version: 3,\\n500|      styles: [{ id: \\\"orchestral\\\", name: \\\"Orquesta\\\" }],\\n(more lines below)\",\"final_result\":true,\"kind\":\"output\",\"task_id\":\"01a18013-9573-7a92-8fed-02ca5fc9eb36\"},\"kind\":\"task_lifecycle\",\"run_stream\":{\"id\":\"01a18013-60b1-7551-82e2-1b1f3ccd850e\",\"kind\":\"run\"},\"task_id\":\"01a18013-9573-7a92-8fed-02ca5fc9eb36\",\"task_stream\":{\"id\":\"01a18013-9573-7a92-8fed-02ca5fc9eb36\",\"kind\":\"task\"}}}\nagent-logs/06-review.jsonl:210:{\"schema_version\":1,\"id\":\"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c4ef\",\"stream\":{\"kind\":\"session\",\"id\":\"01a18013-5db9-7772-9613-fed1b45db42e\"},\"sequence\":210,\"recorded_at\":1780531400000415,\"record_type\":\"event\",\"durability\":\"durable\",\"causation_id\":\"01a18013-60b1-7551-82e2-1b1f3ccd850e\",\"payload_type\":\"tool.result\",\"payload_schema_version\":1,\"payload\":{\"call_id\":\"call_01a180138f57778f9c4b05d83230c532\",\"command_id\":\"01a18013-60b1-7551-82e2-1b1f3ccd850e\",\"correlation_facts\":{\"outcome\":\"success\",\"tool_name\":\"read_file\"},\"kind\":\"tool_result\",\"run_stream\":{\"id\":\"01a18013-60b1-7551-82e2-1b1f3ccd850e\",\"kind\":\"run\"},\"text\":\"Read text file `core/music.ts`.\\n1|// Track selection and manifest parsing. Pure: no env, no fetch, no audio.\\n2|import { EMOTIONS } from \\\"./types\\\";\\n3|import type { EmotionId, Vector8 } from \\\"./types\\\";\\n4|import { buildFeatures } from \\\"./cluster\\\";\\n5|\\n6|// Hand label for the track: the single emotion it was made to carry.\\n7|export type TrackSource = \\\"generated\\\" | \\\"jamendo\\\" | \\\"recording\\\";\\n8|\\n9|export interface Playlist {\\n10|  id: string;\\n11|  label: string;\\n12|  trackIds: string[];\\n13|}\\n14|\\n15|// Fixed id for the owner-requested Chopin playlist. The player button\\n16|// uses the playlist with this id and shows its label verbatim.\\n17|export const CHOPIN_PLAYLIST_ID = \\\"just-play-chopin\\\";\\n18|\\n19|export interface Track {\\n20|  id: string;\\n21|  src: string;\\n22|  title: string;\\n23|  playlistOnly?: boolean;\\n24|  emotion: EmotionId;\\n25|  vector: Vector8;\\n26|  intensity: number;\\n27|  tempo: number;\\n28|  durationSec: number;\\n29|  startSec: number;\\n30|  loop: boolean;\\n31|  soundtrack: string;\\n32|  style: string;\\n33|  source?: TrackSource;\\n34|  artist?: string;\\n35|  composer?: string;\\n36|  license?: string;\\n37|  attribution?: string;\\n38|  sourceUrl?: string;\\n39|}\\n40|\\n41|export interface StyleInfo {\\n42|  id: string;\\n43|  name: string;\\n44|}\\n45|\\n46|export interface Soundtrack {\\n47|  id: string;\\n48|  name: string;\\n49|  style: string;\\n50|  credit?: string;\\n51|}\\n52|\\n53|export interface MusicManifest {\\n54|  version: number;\\n55|  styles: StyleInfo[];\\n56|  soundtracks: Soundtrack[];\\n57|  tracks: Track[];\\n58|  playlists: Playlist[];\\n59|}\\n60|\\n61|// Session selection: style scopes every pick, soundtrackId is the home\\n62|// in soundtrack mode, mode picks the ranking rule.\\n63|export interface MusicSelection {\\n64|  mode: \\\"soundtrack\\\" | \\\"random\\\";\\n65|  soundtrackId: string | null;\\n66|  style: string | null;\\n67|}\\n68|\\n69|export type Rng = () => number;\\n70|\\n71|export interface SelectEnv {\\n72|  selection: MusicSelection;\\n73|  rng: Rng;\\n74|}\\n75|\\n76|export interface PersistedMusicPrefs {\\n77|  mode: \\\"soundtrack\\\" | \\\"random\\\";\\n78|  soundtrackId: string | null;\\n79|  style: string | null;\\n80|}\\n81|\\n82|export interface SceneSignal {\\n83|  vector: Vector8;\\n84|  intensity: number;\\n85|  tempo: number;\\n86|}\\n87|\\n88|export type Similarity = (scene: SceneSignal, track: Track, weights: MusicWeights) => number;\\n89|\\n90|export interface MusicWeights {\\n91|  emotion: number;\\n92|  intensity: number;\\n93|  tempo: number;\\n94|}\\n95|\\n96|export interface MusicConfig {\\n97|  similarity: Similarity;\\n98|  weights: MusicWeights;\\n99|  switchMargin: number;\\n100|  dwellSec: number;\\n101|  minTrackSec: number;\\n102|  hardCutMargin: number;\\n103|  crossfadeSec: number;\\n104|  hardCutCrossfadeSec: number;\\n105|  randomTolerance: number;\\n106|}\\n107|\\n108|// Renormalize the 8 entries to sum 1. Extra keys (such as a Jev\\n109|// \\\"unknown\\\" entry) are ignored. An all-zero vector stays all zero.\\n110|export function normalize8(vector: Record<string, number>): number[] {\\n111|  const values = EMOTIONS.map((id: EmotionId) => {\\n112|    const v = vector[id];\\n113|    return typeof v === \\\"number\\\" && Number.isFinite(v) ? v : 0;\\n114|  });\\n115|  const sum = values.reduce((a, b) => a + b, 0);\\n116|  if (sum <= 0) return values.map(() => 0);\\n117|  return values.map((v) => v / sum);\\n118|}\\n119|\\n120|// Bhattacharyya affinity over the renormalized shapes, plus separate\\n121|// intensity and tempo terms. Fair to blended scenes, unlike cosine.\\n122|export function bhattacharyyaSimilarity(\\n123|  scene: SceneSignal,\\n124|  track: Track,\\n125|  weights: MusicWeights = MUSIC_CONFIG.weights,\\n126|): number {\\n127|  const s = normalize8(scene.vector);\\n128|  const t = normalize8(track.vector);\\n129|  let affinity = 0;\\n130|  for (let i = 0; i < s.length; i++) {\\n131|    affinity += Math.sqrt((s[i] ?? 0) * (t[i] ?? 0));\\n132|  }\\n133|  return (\\n134|    weights.emotion * affinity +\\n135|    weights.intensity * (1 - Math.abs(scene.intensity - track.intensity)) +\\n136|    weights.tempo * (1 - Math.abs(scene.tempo - track.tempo))\\n137|  );\\n138|}\\n139|\\n140|// Cosine over buildFeatures output (vector plus weighted intensity and\\n141|// tempo). Kept as an alternative; it favors peaky scenes.\\n142|export function cosineSimilarity(scene: SceneSignal, track: Track): number {\\n143|  const a = buildFeatures(scene);\\n144|  const b = buildFeatures(track);\\n145|  let dot = 0;\\n146|  let na = 0;\\n147|  let nb = 0;\\n148|  for (let i = 0; i < a.length; i++) {\\n149|    const x = a[i] ?? 0;\\n150|    const y = b[i] ?? 0;\\n151|    dot += x * y;\\n152|    na += x * x;\\n153|    nb += y * y;\\n154|  }\\n155|  if (na === 0 || nb === 0) return 0;\\n156|  return dot / (Math.sqrt(na) * Math.sqrt(nb));\\n157|}\\n158|\\n159|export const MUSIC_CONFIG: MusicConfig = {\\n160|  similarity: bhattacharyyaSimilarity,\\n161|  weights: { emotion: 0.7, intensity: 0.15, tempo: 0.15 },\\n162|  switchMargin: 0.07,\\n163|  dwellSec: 20,\\n164|  minTrackSec: 45,\\n165|  hardCutMargin: 0.2,\\n166|  crossfadeSec: 3,\\n167|  hardCutCrossfadeSec: 1.5,\\n168|  // Admits near ties into the random-mode draw without letting clearly\\n169|  // worse matches in.\\n170|  randomTolerance: 0.05,\\n171|};\\n172|\\n173|export function resolveConfig(override?: Partial<MusicConfig>): MusicConfig {\\n174|  if (!override) return MUSIC_CONFIG;\\n175|  return {\\n176|    ...MUSIC_CONFIG,\\n177|    ...override,\\n178|    weights: override.weights ?? MUSIC_CONFIG.weights,\\n179|  };\\n180|}\\n181|\\n182|export function scoreTrack(\\n183|  scene: SceneSignal,\\n184|  track: Track,\\n185|  override?: Partial<MusicConfig>,\\n186|): number {\\n187|  const config = resolveConfig(override);\\n188|  return config.similarity(scene, track, config.weights);\\n189|}\\n190|\\n191|// Best score first. Ties go to the lower track id, so ranking is stable.\\n192|export function rankTracks(\\n193|  scene: SceneSignal,\\n194|  manifest: MusicManifest,\\n195|  override?: Partial<MusicConfig>,\\n196|): Track[] {\\n197|  const config = resolveConfig(override);\\n198|  return [...manifest.tracks].sort((a, b) => {\\n199|    const diff =\\n200|      config.similarity(scene, b, config.weights) - config.similarity(scene, a, config.weights);\\n201|    if (diff !== 0) return diff;\\n202|    return a.id < b.id ? -1 : a.id > b.id ? 1 : 0;\\n203|  });\\n204|}\\n205|\\n206|// Dominant emotion of a scene: argmax of the renormalized vector, with\\n207|// ties broken by EMOTIONS order.\\n208|export function dominantEmotion(scene: SceneSignal): EmotionId {\\n209|  const norm = normalize8(scene.vector);\\n210|  let best: EmotionId = EMOTIONS[0] as EmotionId;\\n211|  let bestValue = -Infinity;\\n212|  EMOTIONS.forEach((id: EmotionId, i: number) => {\\n213|    const value = norm[i] ?? 0;\\n214|    if (value > bestValue) {\\n215|      bestValue = value;\\n216|      best = id;\\n217|    }\\n218|  });\\n219|  return best;\\n220|}\\n221|\\n222|// Reader skip rule: cycle tracks hand-labeled with the scene's dominant\\n223|// emotion, in score order, wrapping and skipping the current track. When\\n224|// the current track has another emotion, start at the top candidate. With\\n225|// no other same-emotion track, fall back to the best track overall that\\n226|// Style scope for every pick. A null style means the whole manifest,\\n227|// which only happens before the reader resolves the session style.\\n228|// Style scope for every pick, minus playlist-only tracks. Playlist tracks\\n229|// never enter emotion selection, so the filter lives here, not in callers.\\n230|export function candidatesFor(selection: MusicSelection, manifest: MusicManifest): Track[] {\\n231|  const audible = manifest.tracks.filter((t) => t.playlistOnly !== true);\\n232|  if (selection.style === null) return audible;\\n233|  return audible.filter((t) => t.style === selection.style);\\n234|}\\n235|\\n236|// Home set in soundtrack mode: the session soundtrack, or the whole\\n237|// style set when none is set yet.\\n238|export function homeTracks(selection: MusicSelection, styleTracks: Track[]): Track[] {\\n239|  if (selection.soundtrackId === null) return styleTracks;\\n240|  const home = styleTracks.filter((t) => t.soundtrack === selection.soundtrackId);\\n241|  return home.length > 0 ? home : styleTracks;\\n242|}\\n243|\\n244|// \\\"Cambiar track\\\": the next same-emotion track in score order, wrapping\\n245|// and skipping the current. In soundtrack mode it stays inside the\\n246|// current track's soundtrack first, then tries the same emotion in other\\n247|// same-style soundtracks, then the best same-style track overall. In\\n248|// random mode it ranges over all same-style soundtracks at once. A null\\n249|// scene cycles the style set in id order. One track or none gives null.\\n250|export function nextTrack(\\n251|  scene: SceneSignal | null,\\n252|  manifest: MusicManifest,\\n253|  currentTrackId: string | null,\\n254|  override?: Partial<MusicConfig>,\\n255|  selection?: MusicSelection | null,\\n256|): Track | null {\\n257|  const scope =\\n258|    selection == null\\n259|      ? manifest.tracks.filter((t) => t.playlistOnly !== true)\\n260|      : candidatesFor(selection, manifest);\\n261|  if (scope.length <= 1) return null;\\n262|  const config = resolveConfig(override);\\n263|  const scoped = { ...manifest, tracks: scope };\\n264|  if (scene === null) {\\n265|    const ids = [...scope].sort((a, b) => (a.id < b.id ? -1 : a.id > b.id ? 1 : 0));\\n266|    const at = ids.findIndex((t) => t.id === currentTrackId);\\n267|    return ids[(at + 1) % ids.length] as Track;\\n268|  }\\n269|  const ranked = rankTracks(scene, scoped, config);\\n270|  const same = ranked.filter((t) => t.emotion === dominantEmotion(scene));\\n271|  const others = same.filter((t) => t.id !== currentTrackId);\\n272|  if (others.length > 0) {\\n273|    if (selection?.mode === \\\"random\\\") {\\n274|      const at = same.findIndex((t) => t.id === currentTrackId);\\n275|      if (at >= 0) return same[(at + 1) % same.length] as Track;\\n276|      return same[0] as Track;\\n277|    }\\n278|    const current = scope.find((t) => t.id === currentTrackId) ?? null;\\n279|    const home = current ? same.filter((t) => t.soundtrack === current.soundtrack) : [];\\n280|    const homeOthers = home.filter((t) => t.id !== currentTrackId);\\n281|    if (homeOthers.length > 0) {\\n282|      const at = home.findIndex((t) => t.id === currentTrackId);\\n283|      if (at >= 0) return home[(at + 1) % home.length] as Track;\\n284|      return home[0] as Track;\\n285|    }\\n286|    const at = same.findIndex((t) => t.id === currentTrackId);\\n287|    if (at >= 0) return same[(at + 1) % same.length] as Track;\\n288|    return same[0] as Track;\\n289|  }\\n290|  return ranked.find((t) => t.id !== currentTrackId) ?? null;\\n291|}\\n292|\\n293|// Random mode draw: same-style tracks with the scene's dominant emotion\\n294|// (or the whole style set when none matches), scored, kept within\\n295|// randomTolerance of the best. The current track stays when eligible;\\n296|// otherwise the draw skips it when an alternative exists.\\n297|export function pickRandomTrack(\\n298|  cands: Track[],\\n299|  scene: SceneSignal | null,\\n300|  excludeId: string | null,\\n301|  rng: Rng,\\n302|  override?: Partial<MusicConfig>,\\n303|): Track | null {\\n304|  if (cands.length === 0) return null;\\n305|  if (scene === null) {\\n306|    const ids = [...cands].sort((a, b) => (a.id < b.id ? -1 : a.id > b.id ? 1 : 0));\\n307|    const at = ids.findIndex((t) => t.id === excludeId);\\n308|    return ids[(at + 1) % ids.length] as Track;\\n309|  }\\n310|  const config = resolveConfig(override);\\n311|  const scoped = { version: 3, styles: [], soundtracks: [], playlists: [], tracks: cands };\\n312|  const ranked = rankTracks(scene, scoped, config);\\n313|  const dom = dominantEmotion(scene);\\n314|  const pool = ranked.filter((t) => t.emotion === dom);\\n315|  const kept = (pool.length > 0 ? pool : ranked).map((t) => ({\\n316|    track: t,\\n317|    score: config.similarity(scene, t, config.weights),\\n318|  }));\\n319|  const best = kept[0]?.score ?? 0;\\n320|  const eligible = kept.filter((e) => e.score >= best - config.randomTolerance);\\n321|  const current = excludeId !== null ? eligible.find((e) => e.track.id === excludeId) : undefined;\\n322|  if (current) return current.track;\\n323|  const rest = eligible.filter((e) => e.track.id !== excludeId);\\n324|  const drawFrom = rest.length > 0 ? rest : eligible;\\n325|  if (drawFrom.length === 0) return null;\\n326|  return (drawFrom[Math.floor(rng() * drawFrom.length)] as { track: Track }).track;\\n327|}\\n328|\\n329|// Distinct hand-labeled emotions on a soundtrack, ignoring playlist-only\\n330|// tracks. The initial session soundtrack is the one covering most\\n331|// emotions, ties by lower id.\\n332|export function soundtrackCoverage(manifest: MusicManifest, soundtrackId: string): number {\\n333|  return new Set(\\n334|    manifest.tracks\\n335|      .filter((t) => t.soundtrack === soundtrackId && t.playlistOnly !== true)\\n336|      .map((t) => t.emotion),\\n337|  ).size;\\n338|}\\n339|\\n340|export function pickInitialSoundtrack(\\n341|  manifest: MusicManifest,\\n342|  persistedId: string | null,\\n343|): string | null {\\n344|  if (persistedId !== null && manifest.soundtracks.some((s) => s.id === persistedId)) {\\n345|    return persistedId;\\n346|  }\\n347|  let best: string | null = null;\\n348|  let bestCover = -1;\\n349|  for (const s of manifest.soundtracks) {\\n350|    if (!manifest.tracks.some((t) => t.soundtrack === s.id && t.playlistOnly !== true)) continue;\\n351|    const cover = soundtrackCoverage(manifest, s.id);\\n352|    if (cover > bestCover || (cover === bestCover && (best === null || s.id < best))) {\\n353|      best = s.id;\\n354|      bestCover = cover;\\n355|    }\\n356|  }\\n357|  return best;\\n358|}\\n359|\\n360|// True when the style has at least one emotion-selectable track. The style\\n361|// selector uses this, so a style with only playlist tracks stays hidden.\\n362|export function styleHasTracks(manifest: MusicManifest, style: string): boolean {\\n363|  return manifest.tracks.some((t) => t.style === style && t.playlistOnly !== true);\\n364|}\\n365|\\n366|// Session defaults on load. A stored style with no tracks and a stored\\n367|// soundtrack outside the stored style both fall back to the defaults.\\n368|export function resolveInitialSelection(\\n369|  manifest: MusicManifest,\\n370|  persisted: PersistedMusicPrefs | null,\\n371|): MusicSelection {\\n372|  const fallbackId = pickInitialSoundtrack(manifest, null);\\n373|  const fallbackStyle =\\n374|    fallbackId !== null\\n375|      ? (manifest.soundtracks.find((s) => s.id === fallbackId)?.style ?? null)\\n376|      : null;\\n377|  const style =\\n378|    persisted?.style !== null &&\\n379|    persisted?.style !== undefined &&\\n380|    styleHasTracks(manifest, persisted.style)\\n381|      ? persisted.style\\n382|      : fallbackStyle;\\n383|  let soundtrackId: string | null = null;\\n384|  if (style !== null) {\\n385|    const inStyle = (id: string) =>\\n386|      manifest.soundtracks.some((s) => s.id === id && s.style === style);\\n387|    if (\\n388|      persisted?.soundtrackId !== null &&\\n389|      persisted?.soundtrackId !== undefined &&\\n390|      inStyle(persisted.soundtrackId)\\n391|    ) {\\n392|      soundtrackId = persisted.soundtrackId;\\n393|    } else {\\n394|      let best: string | null = null;\\n395|      let bestCover = -1;\\n396|      for (const s of manifest.soundtracks.filter((s) => s.style === style)) {\\n397|        if (!manifest.tracks.some((t) => t.soundtrack === s.id && t.playlistOnly !== true)) {\\n398|          continue;\\n399|        }\\n400|        const cover = soundtrackCoverage(manifest, s.id);\\n401|        if (cover > bestCover || (cover === bestCover && (best === null || s.id < best))) {\\n402|          best = s.id;\\n403|          bestCover = cover;\\n404|        }\\n405|      }\\n406|      soundtrackId = best;\\n407|    }\\n408|  }\\n409|  return {\\n410|    mode: persisted?.mode === \\\"random\\\" ? \\\"random\\\" : \\\"soundtrack\\\",\\n411|    soundtrackId,\\n412|    style,\\n413|  };\\n414|}\\n415|\\n416|// Style change from user action: the session soundtrack becomes the best\\n417|// coverage soundtrack in the new style, and the track is the best match\\n418|// for the scene within the new style. Never crosses styles. Null when\\n419|// the style has no tracks.\\n420|export function requestStyleChange(\\n421|  manifest: MusicManifest,\\n422|  style: string,\\n423|  scene: SceneSignal | null,\\n424|  override?: Partial<MusicConfig>,\\n425|): { soundtrackId: string; track: Track } | null {\\n426|  const scoped = manifest.tracks.filter((t) => t.style === style && t.playlistOnly !== true);\\n427|  if (scoped.length === 0) return null;\\n428|  const config = resolveConfig(override);\\n429|  const inStyle = manifest.soundtracks.filter(\\n430|    (s) => s.style === style && scoped.some((t) => t.soundtrack === s.id),\\n431|  );\\n432|  let soundtrackId = inStyle[0]?.id ?? scoped[0]?.soundtrack ?? \\\"\\\";\\n433|  let bestCover = -1;\\n434|  for (const s of inStyle) {\\n435|    const cover = soundtrackCoverage(manifest, s.id);\\n436|    if (cover > bestCover || (cover === bestCover && s.id < soundtrackId)) {\\n437|      soundtrackId = s.id;\\n438|      bestCover = cover;\\n439|    }\\n440|  }\\n441|  const scopedManifest = { ...manifest, tracks: scoped };\\n442|  let track: Track;\\n443|  if (scene === null) {\\n444|    track = [...scoped].sort((a, b) => (a.id < b.id ? -1 : a.id > b.id ? 1 : 0))[0] as Track;\\n445|  } else {\\n446|    track = rankTracks(scene, scopedManifest, config)[0] as Track;\\n447|  }\\n448|  return { soundtrackId, track };\\n449|}\\n450|\\n451|const SUPPORTED_VERSION = 3;\\n452|const SOURCES = [\\\"generated\\\", \\\"jamendo\\\", \\\"recording\\\"] as const;\\n453|const SLUG = /^[a-z0-9-]+$/;\\n454|\\n455|function isRecord(value: unknown): value is Record<string, unknown> {\\n456|  return typeof value === \\\"object\\\" && value !== null && !Array.isArray(value);\\n457|}\\n458|\\n459|function isOneOf<T extends string>(value: unknown, allowed: readonly T[]): value is T {\\n460|  return typeof value === \\\"string\\\" && allowed.some((entry) => entry === value);\\n461|}\\n462|\\n463|function isVector8(value: unknown): value is Vector8 {\\n464|  if (!isRecord(value)) return false;\\n465|  return EMOTIONS.every(\\n466|    (id: EmotionId) =>\\n467|      typeof value[id] === \\\"number\\\" &&\\n468|      Number.isFinite(value[id]) &&\\n469|      (value[id] as number) >= 0 &&\\n470|      (value[id] as number) <= 1,\\n471|  );\\n472|}\\n473|\\n474|function isUnit(value: unknown): value is number {\\n475|  return typeof value === \\\"number\\\" && Number.isFinite(value) && value >= 0 && value <= 1;\\n476|}\\n477|\\n478|function isSrc(value: unknown): value is string {\\n479|  return (\\n480|    typeof value === \\\"string\\\" && (value.startsWith(\\\"/music/\\\") || value.startsWith(\\\"https://\\\"))\\n481|  );\\n482|}\\n483|\\n484|function isNonEmptyString(value: unknown): value is string {\\n485|  return typeof value === \\\"string\\\" && value !== \\\"\\\";\\n486|}\\n487|\\n488|// Fail loudly on a bad drop-in manifest so broken files never play quiet.\\n489|export function parseManifest(json: unknown): MusicManifest {\\n490|  if (!isRecord(json)) throw new Error(\\\"manifest must be an object\\\");\\n491|  if (json.version !== 3 && json.version !== 2) {\\n492|    throw new Error(`unsupported manifest version: ${String(json.version)}`);\\n493|  }\\n494|  // A v2 manifest becomes one implicit soundtrack holding every track.\\n495|  if (json.version === 2) {\\n496|    if (!Array.isArray(json.tracks)) throw new Error(\\\"manifest tracks must be an array\\\");\\n497|    const tracks = json.tracks.map((entry, i) => parseTrack(entry, i, \\\"default\\\", \\\"orchestral\\\"));\\n498|    return {\\n499|      version: 3,\\n500|      styles: [{ id: \\\"orchestral\\\", name: \\\"Orquesta\\\" }],\\n(more lines below)\"}}\nagent-logs/06-review.jsonl:376:{\"schema_version\":1,\"id\":\"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c63b\",\"stream\":{\"kind\":\"session\",\"id\":\"01a18013-5db9-7772-9613-fed1b45db42e\"},\"sequence\":376,\"recorded_at\":1780531400000747,\"record_type\":\"event\",\"durability\":\"durable\",\"causation_id\":\"01a18013-60b1-7551-82e2-1b1f3ccd850e\",\"payload_type\":\"task.lifecycle.output\",\"payload_schema_version\":1,\"payload\":{\"command_id\":\"01a18013-60b1-7551-82e2-1b1f3ccd850e\",\"event\":{\"chunk\":\"Read text file `docs/contracts.md`.\\n1|# Contracts\\n2|\\n3|Music generation must never block the reader. Each module below owns one\\n4|job and can be swapped without touching the others. Import direction is\\n5|`core <- server` and `core <- app`. Server and client components never\\n6|import each other. `app/page.tsx` may import `server/books.ts`. Client\\n7|files never do.\\n8|\\n9|## Book data\\n10|\\n11|`data/books/oz/book.json` holds the frozen text: id, title, author,\\n12|`textVersion` hash, chapters with `start_n` and `end_n`, and paragraphs\\n13|with `id`, `ch`, `n`, and `text`. `analysis.json` is the scene source\\n14|the reader consumes: the same scenes plus Jev vectors, the Muse\\n15|override, and the `final` emotion. `scenes.json` is the pipeline\\n16|intermediate that `analysis.json` mirrors. The reader consumes the book\\n17|fields, scene ranges and titles, and the `final` vector with intensity\\n18|and tempo. It never sees `jev`, `muse_override`, or provenance.\\n19|`core/reader.ts` defines `buildReaderModel`, which joins paragraphs to\\n20|scenes by ordinal range and throws on unordered scenes or on paragraphs\\n21|covered zero or two times.\\n22|\\n23|## Music library\\n24|\\n25|The library is a static `public/music/manifest.json`, version 3, fetched\\n26|by the client from `/music/manifest.json`. A static file needs no route,\\n27|ships from the CDN, and swaps by replacing files only. Tracks may be\\n28|several minutes long and are not loops unless marked so. A version 2\\n29|manifest migrates inline to one implicit `default` soundtrack of style\\n30|`orchestral`.\\n31|\\n32|`MusicManifest = { version, styles, soundtracks, tracks }`.\\n33|`StyleInfo = { id, name }` where `id` is a lowercase slug and `name` is\\n34|the Spanish display name. `Soundtrack = { id, name, style }` plus\\n35|optional `credit`. `Track = { id, src, title, emotion, vector,\\n36|intensity, tempo, durationSec, soundtrack, style }` plus optional\\n37|`startSec` (default 0, where playback starts on first play and on each\\n38|loop), `loop` (default true), `source` (`generated`, `jamendo`, or\\n39|`recording`), `artist`, `composer`, `license`, `attribution`, and\\n40|`sourceUrl` (https only). `emotion` is the hand label: one of the 8\\n41|emotion ids in `core/types.ts`. The vector covers the 8 ids with finite\\n42|entries in 0..1. Every track names a soundtrack id, every track style\\n43|matches its soundtrack style, and every style is a listed style id.\\n44|`core/music.ts` owns `parseManifest`, which rejects unknown versions,\\n45|duplicate ids, unknown soundtrack or style ids, style mismatches,\\n46|missing fields, bad vectors, NaN entries, out-of-range numbers,\\n47|`startSec` outside its range, unknown `source` values, a non-boolean\\n48|`playlistOnly`, and any `src`\\n49|that is not a `/music/` path or `https` URL. A soundtrack with no\\n50|tracks parses. The reader calls it on every fetch, so a bad drop-in\\n51|fails loudly in dev. Remote URLs need a `media-src` addition in\\n52|`next.config.ts`.\\n53|\\n54|`Track.playlistOnly` defaults to false. A true value marks a playlist\\n55|only track: it still names a soundtrack and style, but no emotion pick\\n56|ever returns it. `MusicManifest.playlists` holds\\n57|`Playlist = { id, label, trackIds }` entries, most notably\\n58|`just-play-chopin`. A missing key parses as an empty list, and a v2\\n59|migration gives an empty list. Parse rejects duplicate playlist ids,\\n60|empty labels, non-array `trackIds`, and any `trackIds` entry that names\\n61|no track, with the playlist and the id in the message.\\n62|\\n63|## Soundtracks and selection\\n64|\\n65|One soundtrack plays at a time. `MusicSelection = { mode, soundtrackId,\\n66|style }` is the session: `style` scopes every pick, `soundtrackId` is\\n67|the home in `soundtrack` mode, `mode` picks the ranking rule. The style\\n68|is the user's choice, changed with the style selector. The initial\\n69|soundtrack is the one covering the most hand-labeled emotions, ties by\\n70|lower id; a valid persisted id wins. The session persists `{ mode,\\n71|soundtrackId, style }` in localStorage under `lectoria.music.v1`. On\\n72|load a stored style with no tracks and a stored soundtrack outside the\\n73|stored style fall back to the defaults. Storage exceptions never break\\n74|playback.\\n75|\\n76|In `soundtrack` mode each scene scores only the session soundtrack. When\\n77|the soundtrack has no track with the scene emotion, the scheduler borrows\\n78|the best same-style track for that scene only and reports `fallback`, so\\n79|the bar can say `de otra banda sonora`. In `random` mode each scheduled\\n80|select draws among same-style tracks with the scene emotion (or the best\\n81|same-style tracks when the emotion is missing) within `randomTolerance`\\n82|(0.05) of the best score, keeps the current track when it is eligible,\\n83|and avoids an immediate repeat otherwise. Dwell and min-track rules hold\\n84|in both modes. The core never calls `Math.random`; the reader injects it\\n85|and tests pass a seeded stub.\\n86|\\n87|## Change track, mix toggle, style change\\n88|\\n89|`nextTrack` cycles same-emotion tracks in score order, wrapping and\\n90|skipping the current. In `soundtrack` mode it stays inside the current\\n91|soundtrack first, then tries the same emotion in other same-style\\n92|soundtracks, then the best same-style track overall. In `random` mode it\\n93|ranges over all same-style soundtracks at once. A null scene cycles the\\n94|style set in id order.\\n95|\\n96|The `Mezclar bandas` toggle flips `mode`. Turning it off keeps the\\n97|soundtrack of the playing track. `requestStyleChange` moves the session\\n98|to the best-coverage soundtrack of the new style and picks the best\\n99|match for the scene there, or the best same-style track by score when the\\n100|style lacks the scene emotion. It never crosses styles. The scheduler\\n101|applies it at once with the normal crossfade and holds the choice like a\\n102|Next. There is no soundtrack-change button.\\n103|\\n104|## Playlist mode\\n105|\\n106|`SchedulerState.playlist` holds `{ id, index }` while a fixed playlist\\n107|plays. `enterPlaylist` switches at once to the first `trackIds` entry\\n108|with `crossfadeSec`, no dwell and no min-track rule. While it is on,\\n109|scene changes update the active scene but never switch, `requestNext`\\n110|and `noteTrackEnded` advance to the next entry in order and wrap from\\n111|the last to the first, and playlist tracks run to their end because the\\n112|player forces looping off. `exitPlaylist` clears the playlist state and\\n113|switches at once to the best match for the current scene under the\\n114|restored selection. The mode is never persisted, so a reload returns to\\n115|emotion mode. The mix toggle and the style selector stay disabled while\\n116|it is on, and the style list hides styles with only playlist tracks.\\n117|\\n118|## Similarity and config\\n119|\\n120|`Similarity = (scene, track, weights) => number`, where\\n121|`SceneSignal = { vector, intensity, tempo }`. The default is\\n122|`bhattacharyyaSimilarity`: both 8-emotion vectors renormalize to sum 1\\n123|(an all-zero vector gives an affinity of 0), `E` is the sum of\\n124|`sqrt(s_k * t_k)`, and the score is `weights.emotion * E` plus\\n125|`weights.intensity` and `weights.tempo` each for intensity and tempo\\n126|closeness. Scoring and ranking pass the resolved config weights in, so\\n127|a weights override changes the ranking. `cosineSimilarity` over\\n128|`buildFeatures` output stays as an exported alternative. One exported object,\\n129|`MUSIC_CONFIG`, holds `similarity`, `weights`, `switchMargin` (0.07),\\n130|`dwellSec` (20), `minTrackSec` (45), `hardCutMargin` (0.20),\\n131|`crossfadeSec` (3), and `hardCutCrossfadeSec` (1.5). Everything else\\n132|reads from it. Ranking ties go to the lower track id.\\n133|\\n134|## Selection scheduler\\n135|\\n136|`core/music-schedule.ts` is a pure state machine. The reader calls\\n137|`observeScene`, `tickScheduler`, `requestNext`, and `noteTrackEnded`\\n138|with explicit `nowSec` values, so all timing is testable without\\n139|timers. State holds the current track id and when it started, the active\\n140|scene id, the pending scene id and since when, and the skip override\\n141|with the scene it belongs to.\\n142|\\n143|A newly entered scene becomes pending and the dwell clock restarts, so\\n144|fast scrolling keeps only the newest scene. The first track ever plays\\n145|at once with no dwell. After the pending scene holds for `dwellSec` it\\n146|becomes active and the override clears. Then the best track switches in\\n147|only when it beats the current score by `switchMargin` and the current\\n148|track played `minTrackSec`, unless it wins by `hardCutMargin` (hard\\n149|cut, short fade). A second passes the active scene back through the\\n150|switch check, so a hold from `minTrackSec` releases on time, unless a\\n151|skip override stands: ticks return no change while it is set, and only\\n152|a new scene promotion clears it. A switch\\n153|reports its crossfade length: 3 s normally,\\n154|1.5 s for hard cuts. The skip choice holds until the next scene change;\\n155|after that, dwell and hysteresis apply with the override track as the\\n156|current track. A null scene means a failed analysis with no vector, so\\n157|it never triggers a switch. A non-looping track that ends fades into\\n158|the best remaining track, excluding the one that ended, and clears the\\n159|skip override.\\n160|\\n161|## Change track\\n162|\\n163|`nextTrack` cycles tracks hand-labeled with the scene dominant emotion\\n164|(argmax of the renormalized scene vector, ties by emotion order), ranked\\n165|by score with ties by lower id, wrapping around and skipping the current\\n166|track. When the current track has another emotion, it starts at the top\\n167|candidate. With no other same-emotion track it falls back to the best\\n168|track overall that is not current. A null scene cycles all tracks in id\\n169|order. One track or none gives null, and the UI disables the button.\\n170|\\n171|## Player\\n172|\\n173|`app/player.tsx` takes the track, the fade length for the latest switch,\\n174|the scene title, a skip flag, and callbacks. It owns two `audio`\\n175|elements, play state, volume, and the equal-power crossfade\\n176|(cos/sin gains over the fade time, driven by `requestAnimationFrame`).\\n177|It never uses the `loop` attribute. Volume lives in a ref, so the slider\\n178|never re-runs the track effect or touches `src`. A new track request\\n179|mid-fade cancels the pending fade and fades from the audible element to\\n180|the newest track. On load each track seeks to `startSec` once metadata\\n181|is available. Long tracks with `loop` true crossfade into the other\\n182|element playing the same track from `startSec` when `currentTime`\\n183|reaches `duration - fade`, where `fade` is the latest scheduler fade\\n184|length, or the config `crossfadeSec` when none was reported yet. When\\n185|`loop` is false the player reports the end and the scheduler picks the\\n186|next-best track excluding the ended one. Pause stops both elements and\\n187|freezes the fade in place; play resumes the audible elements from the\\n188|frozen point. Audio starts once, on the first press, with fade 0.\\n189|Audio starts only after the user presses play. Reduced motion is read in\\n190|state with a change listener and affects visuals only, never the fade.\\n191|\\n192|The bar shows Play/Pause, Volume, a Cambiar track button (disabled when\\n193|Next has nothing to offer), a Mezclar bandas toggle with `aria-pressed`,\\n194|and a style selector listing only styles that have tracks (hidden while\\n195|fewer than two qualify). A `Just play Chopin` toggle appears only when\\n196|the manifest defines that playlist with tracks; its text comes from the\\n197|playlist label, it carries `aria-pressed`, and it shows the Meta blue\\n198|accent while pressed. It shows the track title with its emotion\\n199|label, the soundtrack name, and attribution when present: composer or\\n200|artist, license, and a source link. While the playlist plays, the bar\\n201|hides the emotion label and the fallback note. A fallback pick adds the\\n202|quiet note\\n203|`de otra banda sonora`. On manifest failure the reader still renders and\\n204|the bar shows a short neutral note. UI motion stays under 200 ms.\\n205|Controls are real buttons and inputs with labels, visible focus, and\\n206|keyboard use. `app/player.tsx` keeps the audio engine and bar layout;\\n207|`app/player-controls.tsx` holds the buttons and the style selector;\\n208|`app/music-prefs.ts` owns the storage helper.\\n209|\\n210|## Image api\\n211|\\n212|Contract only, no routes. Request `{ bookId, textVersion, firstN, lastN\\n213|}` names the selection by touched paragraph ordinals. Response `{ url }`\\n214|is a Vercel Blob URL. The cache key is `firstN..lastN` plus\\n215|`textVersion` plus `promptVersion` at a deterministic Blob path with\\n216|`addRandomSuffix: false`. The server checks the path with `head()`\\n217|before generating and never returns bytes. The same paragraph range\\n218|reuses the image. Types live in `core/types.ts`.\\n219|\\n220|## Chat api\\n221|\\n222|Contract only, no routes. Request `{ bookId, textVersion, positionN,\\n223|spoilerMode, messages }` carries the chat history and the reader\\n224|position. The response is streamed text. The server builds context from\\n225|the book text up to `positionN`, or the whole book when `spoilerMode` is\\n226|on, with the book prefix first and the question last so readers share\\n227|the prompt cache. The system prompt answers only from that text and\\n228|refuses the rest. Types live in `core/types.ts`.\\n229|\\n230|## Quotas and budget\\n231|\\n232|Server only. Spend is counted in integer micro-dollars: reserve with\\n233|Redis `INCRBY` before each model call, refund with `DECRBY` after, one\\n234|reserve per call including retries. The server clamps every model tool\\n235|argument. Clients never see keys or raw errors. Generic messages go to\\n236|the client, details stay in server logs.\",\"final_result\":true,\"kind\":\"output\",\"task_id\":\"01a18013-b73c-76f0-a4c9-edca740b3c6d\"},\"kind\":\"task_lifecycle\",\"run_stream\":{\"id\":\"01a18013-60b1-7551-82e2-1b1f3ccd850e\",\"kind\":\"run\"},\"task_id\":\"01a18013-b73c-76f0-a4c9-edca740b3c6d\",\"task_stream\":{\"id\":\"01a18013-b73c-76f0-a4c9-edca740b3c6d\",\"kind\":\"task\"}}}\nagent-logs/06-review.jsonl:381:{\"schema_version\":1,\"id\":\"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c645\",\"stream\":{\"kind\":\"session\",\"id\":\"01a18013-5db9-7772-9613-fed1b45db42e\"},\"sequence\":381,\"recorded_at\":1780531400000757,\"record_type\":\"event\",\"durability\":\"durable\",\"causation_id\":\"01a18013-60b1-7551-82e2-1b1f3ccd850e\",\"payload_type\":\"tool.result\",\"payload_schema_version\":1,\"payload\":{\"call_id\":\"call_01a18013b30973649f35ee4859131258\",\"command_id\":\"01a18013-60b1-7551-82e2-1b1f3ccd850e\",\"correlation_facts\":{\"outcome\":\"success\",\"tool_name\":\"read_file\"},\"kind\":\"tool_result\",\"run_stream\":{\"id\":\"01a18013-60b1-7551-82e2-1b1f3ccd850e\",\"kind\":\"run\"},\"text\":\"Read text file `docs/contracts.md`.\\n1|# Contracts\\n2|\\n3|Music generation must never block the reader. Each module below owns one\\n4|job and can be swapped without touching the others. Import direction is\\n5|`core <- server` and `core <- app`. Server and client components never\\n6|import each other. `app/page.tsx` may import `server/books.ts`. Client\\n7|files never do.\\n8|\\n9|## Book data\\n10|\\n11|`data/books/oz/book.json` holds the frozen text: id, title, author,\\n12|`textVersion` hash, chapters with `start_n` and `end_n`, and paragraphs\\n13|with `id`, `ch`, `n`, and `text`. `analysis.json` is the scene source\\n14|the reader consumes: the same scenes plus Jev vectors, the Muse\\n15|override, and the `final` emotion. `scenes.json` is the pipeline\\n16|intermediate that `analysis.json` mirrors. The reader consumes the book\\n17|fields, scene ranges and titles, and the `final` vector with intensity\\n18|and tempo. It never sees `jev`, `muse_override`, or provenance.\\n19|`core/reader.ts` defines `buildReaderModel`, which joins paragraphs to\\n20|scenes by ordinal range and throws on unordered scenes or on paragraphs\\n21|covered zero or two times.\\n22|\\n23|## Music library\\n24|\\n25|The library is a static `public/music/manifest.json`, version 3, fetched\\n26|by the client from `/music/manifest.json`. A static file needs no route,\\n27|ships from the CDN, and swaps by replacing files only. Tracks may be\\n28|several minutes long and are not loops unless marked so. A version 2\\n29|manifest migrates inline to one implicit `default` soundtrack of style\\n30|`orchestral`.\\n31|\\n32|`MusicManifest = { version, styles, soundtracks, tracks }`.\\n33|`StyleInfo = { id, name }` where `id` is a lowercase slug and `name` is\\n34|the Spanish display name. `Soundtrack = { id, name, style }` plus\\n35|optional `credit`. `Track = { id, src, title, emotion, vector,\\n36|intensity, tempo, durationSec, soundtrack, style }` plus optional\\n37|`startSec` (default 0, where playback starts on first play and on each\\n38|loop), `loop` (default true), `source` (`generated`, `jamendo`, or\\n39|`recording`), `artist`, `composer`, `license`, `attribution`, and\\n40|`sourceUrl` (https only). `emotion` is the hand label: one of the 8\\n41|emotion ids in `core/types.ts`. The vector covers the \n[tool output bounded: strategy=head, original_bytes=3510468, visible_bytes=100000]\n<system-reminder>\nFull output saved to: /home/box/.local/share/muse/sessions/2026/10/28/01a182c7-1fa3-7740-b1c6-efc1a8b254a1/tool-outputs/01a182c7-91c9-7403-85bf-f8dd1acab465/call_01a182c78ece757a9e87bd2cc3161716-search.txt\nFull output is longer than the visible window.\nUse bash tools like head, tail, cat, sed, or grep to inspect and search the full output.\n</system-reminder>","final_result":true,"kind":"output","task_id":"01a182c7-91c9-7403-85bf-f8dd1acab465"},"kind":"task_lifecycle","run_stream":{"id":"01a182c7-21ae-7563-b8aa-8495f4c7e6b2","kind":"run"},"task_id":"01a182c7-91c9-7403-85bf-f8dd1acab465","task_stream":{"id":"01a182c7-91c9-7403-85bf-f8dd1acab465","kind":"task"}}}
