{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c529","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a182c7-1fa3-7740-b1c6-efc1a8b254a1"},"sequence":239,"recorded_at":1780531400000473,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"01a182c7-21ae-7563-b8aa-8495f4c7e6b2","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"call_id":"call_01a182c78ece757a9e87bd2cc3161716","command_id":"01a182c7-21ae-7563-b8aa-8495f4c7e6b2","correlation_facts":{"outcome":"success","tool_name":"search"},"kind":"tool_result","run_stream":{"id":"01a182c7-21ae-7563-b8aa-8495f4c7e6b2","kind":"run"},"text":"package-lock.json:2324:        \"@playwright/test\": \"^1.51.1\",\ndata/music/labels.json:346:      \"durationSec\": 291.58\napp/globals.css:63:  text-indent: 1.5em;\napp/player.tsx:319:          <rect x=\"11.5\" y=\"3\" width=\"2\" height=\"10\" rx=\"0.5\" />\napp/player.tsx:340:              strokeWidth=\"1.5\"\napp/player.tsx:348:              strokeWidth=\"1.5\"\ndocs/reviews/10.md:59:   (\"1.5 s for hard cuts\"). The code deleted `gatedEvaluate`, so\ndocs/reviews/05.md:14:   Problem: `toggle` pauses only the live element. For 1.5 s after a track change the standby element is the audible one, so pressing pause in that window sets state to paused while audio keeps playing.\ndocs/reviews/05.md:114:3. First press double start: confirmed, conditional on a scheduler switch before first press setting `fadeSec` to 3 or 1.5. Common case (`fadeSec` 0) still reassigns `src` twice.\ndocs/reviews/05.md:124:- Scheduler: first track immediate, 20 s dwell with newest-pending-wins, 0.07 margin boundary tested both sides, 45 s min-track with 1.5 s hard-cut exception, null scene promotes without switching.\ndocs/reviews/external-opus-music-selection.md:79:| Crossfade | 3 s normally, 1.5 s for hard cuts; respect reduced-motion only for visuals, not audio |\ndocs/spikes.md:11:| (a) `response_format: url` | 200 | 31.5 s | 982152 | 1600x1600 VP8X | 31245 / 2459 |\ndocs/spikes.md:45:| poppy field | 103 ms | suspenso 0.95 | 2.08, norm 0.52 (0.66) | 1.52, norm 0.38 (0.52) | 848 / 117 |\ndocs/tasks/05-contracts-reader.md:117:playing --track change--> crossfading --1.5s--> playing\ndocs/tasks/05-contracts-reader.md:122:Two `audio` elements fade against each other on change over about 1.5 s, then the old one pauses. `prefers-reduced-motion` sets the fade to 0. Choice: plain audio elements with a volume ramp instead of Web Audio because nothing here needs decoding or filtering, and native elements keep codec and loop behavior free. Loop is on. Audio starts only after the user presses play, which satisfies autoplay rules; track swaps before first press only change `src`. Volume slider sets both elements. UI motion stays under 200 ms per tokens; the audio fade is not UI motion. Controls are real buttons with labels, visible focus, and full keyboard use. The bar shows the track label and the active scene title.\ndocs/contracts.md:52:with no paragraph gaps and a 1.5em first-line indent on following\ndocs/contracts.md:310:credits for today are used up. Come back tomorrow, or bring your own\ndocs/contracts.md:325:counter per UTC day under `DAILY_SPEND_CAP_USD` (default 1.5, 48 h key\nagent-logs/04-impl.jsonl:408:{\"schema_version\":1,\"id\":\"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c67b\",\"stream\":{\"kind\":\"session\",\"id\":\"01a17ee0-a092-7f93-b8fa-5add1afe57e5\"},\"sequence\":408,\"recorded_at\":1780531400000811,\"record_type\":\"event\",\"durability\":\"durable\",\"causation_id\":\"01a17ee0-a1d9-7863-b0fc-80f17b6c0588\",\"payload_type\":\"task.lifecycle.output\",\"payload_schema_version\":1,\"payload\":{\"command_id\":\"01a17ee0-a1d9-7863-b0fc-80f17b6c0588\",\"event\":{\"chunk\":\"{\\n  \\\"chunk_id\\\": \\\"exec-7-1\\\",\\n  \\\"command\\\": \\\"npm install 2>&1 | tail -5\\\",\\n  \\\"description\\\": \\\"Install dev dependencies with npm\\\",\\n  \\\"exit_code\\\": 0,\\n  \\\"terminal_status\\\": \\\"completed\\\",\\n  \\\"output\\\": \\\"npm warn install-scripts 2 packages have install scripts not yet covered by allowScripts:\\\\nnpm warn install-scripts   esbuild@0.28.2 (postinstall: node install.js)\\\\nnpm warn install-scripts   esbuild@0.21.5 (postinstall: node install.js)\\\\nnpm warn install-scripts\\\\nnpm warn install-scripts Run `npm install-scripts ls` to review, or `npm install-scripts approve <pkg>` to allow.\\\\n\\\",\\n  \\\"original_output_bytes\\\": 375,\\n  \\\"original_output_tokens\\\": 94,\\n  \\\"truncated\\\": false\\n}\",\"final_result\":true,\"kind\":\"output\",\"task_id\":\"01a17ee0-ff07-7a20-b5bd-c2c83d5d49b1\"},\"kind\":\"task_lifecycle\",\"run_stream\":{\"id\":\"01a17ee0-a1d9-7863-b0fc-80f17b6c0588\",\"kind\":\"run\"},\"task_id\":\"01a17ee0-ff07-7a20-b5bd-c2c83d5d49b1\",\"task_stream\":{\"id\":\"01a17ee0-ff07-7a20-b5bd-c2c83d5d49b1\",\"kind\":\"task\"}}}\nagent-logs/04-impl.jsonl:410:{\"schema_version\":1,\"id\":\"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c67f\",\"stream\":{\"kind\":\"session\",\"id\":\"01a17ee0-a092-7f93-b8fa-5add1afe57e5\"},\"sequence\":410,\"recorded_at\":1780531400000815,\"record_type\":\"event\",\"durability\":\"durable\",\"causation_id\":\"01a17ee0-a1d9-7863-b0fc-80f17b6c0588\",\"payload_type\":\"tool.result\",\"payload_schema_version\":1,\"payload\":{\"call_id\":\"call_01a17ee0fa74737d9bd5c27bfa2ce0dc\",\"command_id\":\"01a17ee0-a1d9-7863-b0fc-80f17b6c0588\",\"correlation_facts\":{\"outcome\":\"success\",\"tool_name\":\"bash\"},\"kind\":\"tool_result\",\"run_stream\":{\"id\":\"01a17ee0-a1d9-7863-b0fc-80f17b6c0588\",\"kind\":\"run\"},\"text\":\"{\\n  \\\"chunk_id\\\": \\\"exec-7-1\\\",\\n  \\\"command\\\": \\\"npm install 2>&1 | tail -5\\\",\\n  \\\"description\\\": \\\"Install dev dependencies with npm\\\",\\n  \\\"exit_code\\\": 0,\\n  \\\"terminal_status\\\": \\\"completed\\\",\\n  \\\"output\\\": \\\"npm warn install-scripts 2 packages have install scripts not yet covered by allowScripts:\\\\nnpm warn install-scripts   esbuild@0.28.2 (postinstall: node install.js)\\\\nnpm warn install-scripts   esbuild@0.21.5 (postinstall: node install.js)\\\\nnpm warn install-scripts\\\\nnpm warn install-scripts Run `npm install-scripts ls` to review, or `npm install-scripts approve <pkg>` to allow.\\\\n\\\",\\n  \\\"original_output_bytes\\\": 375,\\n  \\\"original_output_tokens\\\": 94,\\n  \\\"truncated\\\": false\\n}\"}}\nagent-logs/06-review.jsonl:52:{\"schema_version\":1,\"id\":\"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c3b3\",\"stream\":{\"kind\":\"session\",\"id\":\"01a18013-5db9-7772-9613-fed1b45db42e\"},\"sequence\":52,\"recorded_at\":1780531400000099,\"record_type\":\"event\",\"durability\":\"durable\",\"causation_id\":\"01a18013-60b1-7551-82e2-1b1f3ccd850e\",\"payload_type\":\"task.lifecycle.output\",\"payload_schema_version\":1,\"payload\":{\"command_id\":\"01a18013-60b1-7551-82e2-1b1f3ccd850e\",\"event\":{\"chunk\":\"Read text file `docs/reviews/05.md`.\\n1|# Review: task 5 contracts and scene reader\\n2|\\n3|Verdict: fix finding 1 first. The reader renders and plays, but slow scrolling never moves the music to the next scene. Findings 2 to 6 should land in the same pass; 7 to 11 are nits.\\n4|\\n5|What this change does: adds the module contracts in `docs/contracts.md`, pure track selection and manifest parsing in `core/music.ts`, the slim reader model in `core/reader.ts`, a server-only Oz loader in `server/books.ts`, and the client reader (`app/reader.tsx`, `app/active-scene.ts`, `app/player.tsx`) with a two-track placeholder manifest in `public/music/`.\\n6|\\n7|## Findings\\n8|\\n9|1. **Slow scroll down never advances the active scene** (blocker), `app/reader.tsx:107-119`, `app/active-scene.ts:10-25`.\\n10|   Problem: the observer callback scores only the changed entries. A new scene enters the 5 percent band from below with its top under the reading line, so `pickActiveScene` skips it. Its top then crosses the line with no further callback (intersection status does not change), and when the old scene exits, the old entry is filtered out and the result falls back to current. The next scene is adopted only when its top is already above the line at entry, which is the scroll-up direction plus jumps, not scroll-down.\\n11|   Fix: use entries only as a trigger and re-snapshot all sections with live rects on each callback, as the mount path already does. Derive the hit flag from rect versus band in the snapshot mapper.\\n12|\\n13|2. **Pause during a crossfade leaves the incoming element playing** (should-fix), `app/player.tsx:61-80`.\\n14|   Problem: `toggle` pauses only the live element. For 1.5 s after a track change the standby element is the audible one, so pressing pause in that window sets state to paused while audio keeps playing.\\n15|   Fix: pause both refs in `toggle`, or keep the fading pair in one ref both handlers use.\\n16|\\n17|3. **Volume sits in the track-effect deps and restarts fades** (should-fix), `app/player.tsx:28-59`.\\n18|   Problem: every slider tick re-runs the track effect. While paused the early return does not apply (live is paused), so each tick reassigns `standby.src` and flips `liveRef`. Mid-fade it also reassigns the incoming `src`, which reloads that track from zero, and starts a fresh interval.\\n19|   Fix: drop `volume` from the deps, read it through a ref inside the fade, and return early when the live element already carries the track `src` regardless of paused state.\\n20|\\n21|4. **Validator accepts NaN vector entries** (should-fix), `core/music.ts:34-37`.\\n22|   Problem: `isVector8` checks `typeof` only, and `typeof NaN` is `number`. A NaN entry passes `parseManifest`, then poisons the cosine score and the sort order for that track.\\n23|   Fix: require `Number.isFinite` for each of the 8 values, one word in the same check.\\n24|\\n25|5. **Tests skip the behaviors the brief asked about** (should-fix), `core/music.test.ts`, `app/reader.tsx:36-61`.\\n26|   Problem: no test covers `nextAlternative` with a null scene, `selectTrack` with an excluded current track, the skip override held until the scene change and then used as current, or reselection when the manifest lands after the first scene. The observer wiring has no test beyond the pure picker.\\n27|   Fix: add the three core cases (null scene alternative, excluded current, excluded all) and pull `applyScene` into a pure helper beside `active-scene.ts` with two tests: override as base on scene change, cleared after.\\n28|\\n29|6. **Doc says the reader consumes `scenes.json`, code never reads it** (should-fix), `docs/contracts.md:11-20`, `server/books.ts:9-17`.\\n30|   Problem: `loadOzBook` reads `book.json` plus `analysis.json` only, which is fine because analysis carries every scene field, but the contract lists `scenes.json` as an input the reader consumes.\\n31|   Fix: name `analysis.json` as the scene source and `scenes.json` as the pipeline intermediate it mirrors, in one sentence.\\n32|\\n33|7. **Tie-break repeats an index scan per comparison** (nit), `core/music.ts:96-99`.\\n34|   Problem: the comparator calls `manifest.tracks.indexOf` on each tie. Sort is already stable, so ties follow manifest order without it.\\n35|   Fix: delete the tie branch and return the diff.\\n36|\\n37|8. **Two `SceneEmotion` types with different shapes** (nit), `core/music.ts:22-26`, `core/types.ts:78-83`.\\n38|   Problem: `core/music.ts` exports `SceneEmotion` as `{ vector, intensity, tempo }` while `core/types.ts` uses the same name for `{ jev, muse_override, final, error }`. Each reads fine alone; importing both invites the wrong one.\\n39|   Fix: rename the music one to `SceneSignal` or reuse an inline param type.\\n40|\\n41|9. **Snapshot helper takes a flag it never varies** (nit), `app/reader.tsx:31, 101-106`.\\n42|   Problem: `snapshot(hit)` is called once with `true`, and `byId.current` is rebuilt on every render.\\n43|   Fix: delete the parameter and build the map with `useMemo` on `scenes`.\\n44|\\n45|10. **Reduced-motion choice never updates** (nit), `app/player.tsx:26`.\\n46|    Problem: `matchMedia` runs per render with no listener, so flipping the OS setting mid session keeps the old fade until a rerender for another reason.\\n47|    Fix: read it once in state with a change listener, or leave it; the wrongness lasts one session at most.\\n48|\\n49|11. **Track swap mid-fade restarts from partial volumes** (nit), `app/player.tsx:43-56`.\\n50|    Problem: the cleanup clears the old interval but leaves the old live element at partial volume, and the new run fades from there while the incoming `src` is replaced. Playback converges, only the fade curve kinks.\\n51|    Fix: nothing required once finding 3 lands; note it only if the effect is reworked anyway.\\n52|\\n53|## Checked and fine\\n54|\\n55|- Core purity: no `process.env`, `node:` imports, `fetch`, or `fs` in `core/` outside tests. Import direction holds: `app/page.tsx` imports `server/books.ts`, client files import only `core/` and siblings, `server/books.ts` starts with `import 'server-only'`.\\n56|- Client payload: only scene ids, titles, and emotion triples pass to `Reader`. `buildReaderModel` spreads `final` (`vector`, `intensity`, `tempo`) and drops `jev`, `muse_override`, provenance. The reader test asserts both internals are absent.\\n57|- Image and chat types match the spec: `{ bookId, textVersion, firstN, lastN }` to `{ url }`, and `{ bookId, textVersion, positionN, spoilerMode, messages }` with `{ role, text }` messages. Contract only, no routes.\\n58|- Manifest trust boundary: the client parses every fetch with `parseManifest`, which rejects unknown versions, missing fields, short vectors, out-of-range numbers, and non-`/music/` non-https `src`. Bad drop-ins fail loudly.\\n59|- CSP unchanged and sufficient: `media-src 'self' blob:` covers the placeholder clips, `connect-src 'self'` covers the manifest fetch. Both docs note remote https tracks need a `media-src` edit.\\n60|- Reading line consistent with the band: the band spans 30 to 35 percent of viewport height, the line sits at one third, inside the band. Short scenes still cross it because sections span their paragraphs.\\n61|- Swap guide: `public/music/README.md` replaces files plus manifest plus version bump, names `parseManifest` as the shape check, and carries the CC-BY-NC non-commercial note. Swap needs no code change.\\n62|- Design: styles use tokens only (all names exist in `app/tokens.css`), accent is Meta blue on borders and focus, no purple or gradients, controls are real buttons and inputs with labels and visible focus, no UI transition over 200 ms (audio fade is not UI motion).\\n63|- Prose: `docs/contracts.md` and the README are short, sentence case, no filler or banned words.\\n64|- Runs: `npm test` 63/63 across 14 files, `npm run typecheck` clean, `npm run build` clean with `/` prerendered static.\\n65|\\n66|## Not checked\\n67|\\n68|- Audible playback, real scroll behavior, and screen-reader pass were not run; the observer finding rests on reading plus band math, not a browser session. Live manifest fetch against the built server was not repeated.\\n69|\\n70|## Round 2\\n71|\\n72|What this change does: the fix pass answers findings 1 to 10, adds manifest v2 with hand-labeled emotions, a pure scheduler with dwell/hysteresis/min-track/hard-cut, same-emotion Next, and a two-element player rewrite with loop crossfades and attribution. The rules all land. Three player/scheduler defects do not.\\n73|\\n74|### Must fix\\n75|\\n76|1. **Reader skip choice reverts on the same scene** (breaks Martin's rule), `core/music-schedule.ts:60-100, 151-166`.\\n77|   Problem: `evaluateSwitch` never reads `overrideId`, and `tickScheduler` re-runs it every second. After Change track the override is a dead field: it is set in `requestNext` (`music-schedule.ts:185-186`) and cleared in `promote`, but nothing checks it.\\n78|   Case (run against the real scheduler): scene pure tristeza, tracks pure/bland tristeza plus calm; Next moves pure to bland with gap 0.145, then `tickScheduler` at 45 s after the press switches back to pure on the same scene, stale `overrideId: bland` still set. Gaps at or above `hardCutMargin` revert within one second instead. The committed fixture hides this only because its same-emotion gaps sit below `switchMargin`.\\n79|   Fix: in `tickScheduler`, when there is no pending scene and `overrideId` is set, return `noChange` without the re-check. Pending promotion still clears the override. Add the missing test: override versus a mid-gap scene holds past `minTrackSec`.\\n80|   If we skip it: the Change track button undoes itself, worst on scenes where the reader's pick scores far below best.\\n81|\\n82|2. **Loop fade restarts on every timeupdate for 3 s** (audible stutter, repeated reloads), `app/player.tsx:86, 145-157`.\\n83|   Problem: `handleTimeUpdate` arms `loopArmedRef` then calls `requestPlayRef`, whose first lines clear `loopArmedRef` back to null. The old element stays `audibleRef` until the fade finishes, so each later timeupdate re-arms, cancels the fade, reassigns `dst.src` (reload), and restarts the fade.\\n84|   Case: any looping track within `crossfadeSec` of its end fires timeupdate about 4 times per second; each one restarts the 3 s loop fade.\\n85|   Fix: delete the unconditional clear at line 86 and clear the arm only on a real track change, e.g. guard it with `trackRef.current?.id !== next.id` before the assignment. One line.\\n86|   If we skip it: every loop point stutters instead of crossfading.\\n87|\\n88|3. **First press can start the same track twice** (self-crossfade), `app/player.tsx:130-141, 174-184`.\\n89|   Problem: first-press `toggle` calls `requestPlay(next, 0)`, then the `[started, trackId]` effect fires on the same track and calls `requestPlay(next, fadeSec)`. When the scheduler already switched pre-press, `fadeSec` can be 3, so the track crossfades into itself on the other element. Even at 0 the `src` is assigned twice.\\n90|   Fix: remove the direct `requestPlay` call from the first-press branch and let the effect do the single start. Note in the diff that a pre-press scheduler switch then gives a 3 s fade-in on first press; force 0 there if Martin wants instant start.\\n91|   If we skip it: readers who read a while before pressing play hear the track restart into itself.\\n92|\\n93|### Should fix\\n94|\\n95|4. **Config override for weights is silently ignored; loop fades bypass the scheduler fade** (one-config rule), `core/music.ts:79-84`, `app/player.tsx:149-168`.\\n96|   Problem: `bhattacharyyaSimilarity` reads `MUSIC_CONFIG.weights` directly, so `rankTracks(scene, m, { weights: custom })` scores with the global weights. Separately, the loop and ended paths hardcode `MUSIC_CONFIG.crossfadeSec` instead of the `fadeSec` prop the scheduler reported, so a custom `crossfadeSec` applies to switches but not loops.\\n97|   Fix: pass `config.weights` into the similarity call in `scoreTrack`/`rankTracks`, and read the loop fade length from `fadeSecRef` instead of the global.\\n98|   If we skip it: tests and future tuning knobs lie about which values are live.\\n99|\\n100|5. **Pause does not freeze the fade** (wrong element resumes), `app/player.tsx:110-127, 185-189`.\\n101|   Problem: pause stops both elements but never cancels or freezes the rAF fade. The tick keeps animating gains and flips `audibleRef` while paused. Resuming mid-fade replays both elements (both levels above 0.02) until the fade converges.\\n102|   Fix: skip the level update while `playingRef` is false and let the scheduled tick continue the fade on resume. Two lines.\\n103|   If we skip it: a pause-resume inside a 3 s fade briefly plays both elements at once.\\n104|\\n105|6. **Ended non-loop track leaves a stale override** (live once finding 1 lands), `core/music-schedule.ts:196-213`.\\n106|   Problem: `noteTrackEnded` correctly updates `currentStartedSec` and excludes the ended id, but keeps the old `overrideId`. Harmless today because nothing reads it; after finding 1 the stale id would wrongly block switches.\\n107|   Fix: clear `overrideId`/`overrideSceneId` in `noteTrackEnded` together with finding 1. The pre-manifest `activeId` versus scheduler divergence (`app/reader.tsx:26, 81-85`) converges on manifest load and needs no change.\\n108|   If we skip it: fixing 1 without this trades one stuck-override bug for another.\\n109|\\n110|### Sequences 1 to 7, verdicts\\n111|\\n112|1. Override overwritten: confirmed. Same scene, gap at or above margin: revert after `minTrackSec` (proven run above); gap at or above `hardCutMargin`: revert within one second. Only the committed fixture's small gaps mask it.\\n113|2. Loop re-trigger: confirmed by reading. The clear at line 86 runs inside every loop-triggered `requestPlay`, so the arm never survives until the fade completes.\\n114|3. First press double start: confirmed, conditional on a scheduler switch before first press setting `fadeSec` to 3 or 1.5. Common case (`fadeSec` 0) still reassigns `src` twice.\\n115|4. Direct `MUSIC_CONFIG.crossfadeSec` in loop/end paths: confirmed for the player loop paths; `noteTrackEnded` correctly uses the resolved config. Weights override dead as described in finding 4.\\n116|5. Pause during fade: confirmed by reading. rAF tick has no `playingRef` gate; pause has no `cancelFade`.\\n117|6. `noteTrackEnded`: updates `currentStartedSec`, ignores the override (finding 6). Reader `activeId` diverges from the scheduler only before the manifest lands and converges through the reselect effect; no fix needed.\\n118|7. Same-emotion Next tests: covered. `core/music.test.ts:116-121` cycle order, wrap, skip current; `:123-126` other-emotion and null current start at top; `:128-140` both fallbacks; `:142-146` null scene id order; `:148-152` one track and none. Scheduler override hold/clear at `core/music-schedule.test.ts:202-218`. Missing only the large-gap override hold (finding 1).\\n119|\\n120|### Checked and fine\\n121|\\n122|- First-review findings 1 to 10 all addressed: observer re-snapshot (`app/reader.tsx:94-98`) with scroll-down, scroll-up, and jump picker tests; pause stops both elements; volume lives in a ref outside the track effect deps; `isVector8` requires finite 0..1 entries; core and picker tests added; contracts names `analysis.json` as the scene source and `scenes.json` as the pipeline intermediate; tie-break by lower id; `SceneSignal` rename; `byId` memo with no flag parameter; reduced-motion listener in state, audio fade always full length. Finding 11 is moot: mid-fade requests cancel and restart from live levels.\\n123|- Manifest v2: version pinned to 2, `title` rename, all required and optional fields with range checks, `startSec` below `durationSec`, `loop` default true, unknown `source` and non-https `sourceUrl` rejected, NaN rejected. Committed manifest parses as v2 with `calma`/`suspenso` hand labels, `generated` source, CC-BY-NC-4.0 license, and MusicGen placeholder attribution.\\n124|- Scheduler: first track immediate, 20 s dwell with newest-pending-wins, 0.07 margin boundary tested both sides, 45 s min-track with 1.5 s hard-cut exception, null scene promotes without switching.\\n125|- Player: no `loop` attribute, `startSec` seek on metadata, non-loop end delegates to the scheduler excluding the ended track, volume never touches `src`, attribution shows composer/artist, license, and source link with `rel=\\\"noopener noreferrer\\\"` and `target _blank`, emotion label shown in Spanish as stored, Change track disabled exactly when `nextTrack` returns null.\\n126|- Core purity holds: no env, `node:`, fetch, or timers in `core/` outside tests. No purple, violet, or gradient in the player or reader.\\n127|- Runs: `npm test` 81/81 across 15 files, `npm run typecheck` clean, `npm run build` clean with `/` prerendered static.\\n128|\\n129|### Not checked\\n130|\\n131|- Audible playback and real scroll behavior were not run. `app/globals.css` and `app/page.tsx` diffs were not reviewed. `npm run test:hooks`, `npm run check:size`, `npm run check:secrets`, and the Modal/Blob paths were not run.\",\"final_result\":true,\"kind\":\"output\",\"task_id\":\"01a18013-6706-7031-a830-dde0960b028c\"},\"kind\":\"task_lifecycle\",\"run_stream\":{\"id\":\"01a18013-60b1-7551-82e2-1b1f3ccd850e\",\"kind\":\"run\"},\"task_id\":\"01a18013-6706-7031-a830-dde0960b028c\",\"task_stream\":{\"id\":\"01a18013-6706-7031-a830-dde0960b028c\",\"kind\":\"task\"}}}\nagent-logs/06-review.jsonl:56:{\"schema_version\":1,\"id\":\"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c3bb\",\"stream\":{\"kind\":\"session\",\"id\":\"01a18013-5db9-7772-9613-fed1b45db42e\"},\"sequence\":56,\"recorded_at\":1780531400000107,\"record_type\":\"event\",\"durability\":\"durable\",\"causation_id\":\"01a18013-60b1-7551-82e2-1b1f3ccd850e\",\"payload_type\":\"tool.result\",\"payload_schema_version\":1,\"payload\":{\"call_id\":\"call_01a1801365d2772985ec7a2e4ab2ad31\",\"command_id\":\"01a18013-60b1-7551-82e2-1b1f3ccd850e\",\"correlation_facts\":{\"outcome\":\"success\",\"tool_name\":\"read_file\"},\"kind\":\"tool_result\",\"run_stream\":{\"id\":\"01a18013-60b1-7551-82e2-1b1f3ccd850e\",\"kind\":\"run\"},\"text\":\"Read text file `docs/reviews/05.md`.\\n1|# Review: task 5 contracts and scene reader\\n2|\\n3|Verdict: fix finding 1 first. The reader renders and plays, but slow scrolling never moves the music to the next scene. Findings 2 to 6 should land in the same pass; 7 to 11 are nits.\\n4|\\n5|What this change does: adds the module contracts in `docs/contracts.md`, pure track selection and manifest parsing in `core/music.ts`, the slim reader model in `core/reader.ts`, a server-only Oz loader in `server/books.ts`, and the client reader (`app/reader.tsx`, `app/active-scene.ts`, `app/player.tsx`) with a two-track placeholder manifest in `public/music/`.\\n6|\\n7|## Findings\\n8|\\n9|1. **Slow scroll down never advances the active scene** (blocker), `app/reader.tsx:107-119`, `app/active-scene.ts:10-25`.\\n10|   Problem: the observer callback scores only the changed entries. A new scene enters the 5 percent band from below with its top under the reading line, so `pickActiveScene` skips it. Its top then crosses the line with no further callback (intersection status does not change), and when the old scene exits, the old entry is filtered out and the result falls back to current. The next scene is adopted only when its top is already above the line at entry, which is the scroll-up direction plus jumps, not scroll-down.\\n11|   Fix: use entries only as a trigger and re-snapshot all sections with live rects on each callback, as the mount path already does. Derive the hit flag from rect versus band in the snapshot mapper.\\n12|\\n13|2. **Pause during a crossfade leaves the incoming element playing** (should-fix), `app/player.tsx:61-80`.\\n14|   Problem: `toggle` pauses only the live element. For 1.5 s after a track change the standby element is the audible one, so pressing pause in that window sets state to paused while audio keeps playing.\\n15|   Fix: pause both refs in `toggle`, or keep the fading pair in one ref both handlers use.\\n16|\\n17|3. **Volume sits in the track-effect deps and restarts fades** (should-fix), `app/player.tsx:28-59`.\\n18|   Problem: every slider tick re-runs the track effect. While paused the early return does not apply (live is paused), so each tick reassigns `standby.src` and flips `liveRef`. Mid-fade it also reassigns the incoming `src`, which reloads that track from zero, and starts a fresh interval.\\n19|   Fix: drop `volume` from the deps, read it through a ref inside the fade, and return early when the live element already carries the track `src` regardless of paused state.\\n20|\\n21|4. **Validator accepts NaN vector entries** (should-fix), `core/music.ts:34-37`.\\n22|   Problem: `isVector8` checks `typeof` only, and `typeof NaN` is `number`. A NaN entry passes `parseManifest`, then poisons the cosine score and the sort order for that track.\\n23|   Fix: require `Number.isFinite` for each of the 8 values, one word in the same check.\\n24|\\n25|5. **Tests skip the behaviors the brief asked about** (should-fix), `core/music.test.ts`, `app/reader.tsx:36-61`.\\n26|   Problem: no test covers `nextAlternative` with a null scene, `selectTrack` with an excluded current track, the skip override held until the scene change and then used as current, or reselection when the manifest lands after the first scene. The observer wiring has no test beyond the pure picker.\\n27|   Fix: add the three core cases (null scene alternative, excluded current, excluded all) and pull `applyScene` into a pure helper beside `active-scene.ts` with two tests: override as base on scene change, cleared after.\\n28|\\n29|6. **Doc says the reader consumes `scenes.json`, code never reads it** (should-fix), `docs/contracts.md:11-20`, `server/books.ts:9-17`.\\n30|   Problem: `loadOzBook` reads `book.json` plus `analysis.json` only, which is fine because analysis carries every scene field, but the contract lists `scenes.json` as an input the reader consumes.\\n31|   Fix: name `analysis.json` as the scene source and `scenes.json` as the pipeline intermediate it mirrors, in one sentence.\\n32|\\n33|7. **Tie-break repeats an index scan per comparison** (nit), `core/music.ts:96-99`.\\n34|   Problem: the comparator calls `manifest.tracks.indexOf` on each tie. Sort is already stable, so ties follow manifest order without it.\\n35|   Fix: delete the tie branch and return the diff.\\n36|\\n37|8. **Two `SceneEmotion` types with different shapes** (nit), `core/music.ts:22-26`, `core/types.ts:78-83`.\\n38|   Problem: `core/music.ts` exports `SceneEmotion` as `{ vector, intensity, tempo }` while `core/types.ts` uses the same name for `{ jev, muse_override, final, error }`. Each reads fine alone; importing both invites the wrong one.\\n39|   Fix: rename the music one to `SceneSignal` or reuse an inline param type.\\n40|\\n41|9. **Snapshot helper takes a flag it never varies** (nit), `app/reader.tsx:31, 101-106`.\\n42|   Problem: `snapshot(hit)` is called once with `true`, and `byId.current` is rebuilt on every render.\\n43|   Fix: delete the parameter and build the map with `useMemo` on `scenes`.\\n44|\\n45|10. **Reduced-motion choice never updates** (nit), `app/player.tsx:26`.\\n46|    Problem: `matchMedia` runs per render with no listener, so flipping the OS setting mid session keeps the old fade until a rerender for another reason.\\n47|    Fix: read it once in state with a change listener, or leave it; the wrongness lasts one session at most.\\n48|\\n49|11. **Track swap mid-fade restarts from partial volumes** (nit), `app/player.tsx:43-56`.\\n50|    Problem: the cleanup clears the old interval but leaves the old live element at partial volume, and the new run fades from there while the incoming `src` is replaced. Playback converges, only the fade curve kinks.\\n51|    Fix: nothing required once finding 3 lands; note it only if the effect is reworked anyway.\\n52|\\n53|## Checked and fine\\n54|\\n55|- Core purity: no `process.env`, `node:` imports, `fetch`, or `fs` in `core/` outside tests. Import direction holds: `app/page.tsx` imports `server/books.ts`, client files import only `core/` and siblings, `server/books.ts` starts with `import 'server-only'`.\\n56|- Client payload: only scene ids, titles, and emotion triples pass to `Reader`. `buildReaderModel` spreads `final` (`vector`, `intensity`, `tempo`) and drops `jev`, `muse_override`, provenance. The reader test asserts both internals are absent.\\n57|- Image and chat types match the spec: `{ bookId, textVersion, firstN, lastN }` to `{ url }`, and `{ bookId, textVersion, positionN, spoilerMode, messages }` with `{ role, text }` messages. Contract only, no routes.\\n58|- Manifest trust boundary: the client parses every fetch with `parseManifest`, which rejects unknown versions, missing fields, short vectors, out-of-range numbers, and non-`/music/` non-https `src`. Bad drop-ins fail loudly.\\n59|- CSP unchanged and sufficient: `media-src 'self' blob:` covers the placeholder clips, `connect-src 'self'` covers the manifest fetch. Both docs note remote https tracks need a `media-src` edit.\\n60|- Reading line consistent with the band: the band spans 30 to 35 percent of viewport height, the line sits at one third, inside the band. Short scenes still cross it because sections span their paragraphs.\\n61|- Swap guide: `public/music/README.md` replaces files plus manifest plus version bump, names `parseManifest` as the shape check, and carries the CC-BY-NC non-commercial note. Swap needs no code change.\\n62|- Design: styles use tokens only (all names exist in `app/tokens.css`), accent is Meta blue on borders and focus, no purple or gradients, controls are real buttons and inputs with labels and visible focus, no UI transition over 200 ms (audio fade is not UI motion).\\n63|- Prose: `docs/contracts.md` and the README are short, sentence case, no filler or banned words.\\n64|- Runs: `npm test` 63/63 across 14 files, `npm run typecheck` clean, `npm run build` clean with `/` prerendered static.\\n65|\\n66|## Not checked\\n67|\\n68|- Audible playback, real scroll behavior, and screen-reader pass were not run; the observer finding rests on reading plus band math, not a browser session. Live manifest fetch against the built server was not repeated.\\n69|\\n70|## Round 2\\n71|\\n72|What this change does: the fix pass answers findings 1 to 10, adds manifest v2 with hand-labeled emotions, a pure scheduler with dwell/hysteresis/min-track/hard-cut, same-emotion Next, and a two-element player rewrite with loop crossfades and attribution. The rules all land. Three player/scheduler defects do not.\\n73|\\n74|### Must fix\\n75|\\n76|1. **Reader skip choice reverts on the same scene** (breaks Martin's rule), `core/music-schedule.ts:60-100, 151-166`.\\n77|   Problem: `evaluateSwitch` never reads `overrideId`, and `tickScheduler` re-runs it every second. After Change track the override is a dead field