{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c8a5","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a182c7-1fa3-7740-b1c6-efc1a8b254a1"},"sequence":685,"recorded_at":1780531400001365,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"01a182c7-21ae-7563-b8aa-8495f4c7e6b2","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"command_id":"01a182c7-21ae-7563-b8aa-8495f4c7e6b2","event":{"chunk":"edited\nchanged lines: lines 306-313\n--- original\n+++ updated\n@@\n-`bad_request` with a friendly English message. Both `budget` and\n-`daily_budget` answer `MSG_CREDITS_OUT` (`core/images.ts`): \"So many\n-people loved this that we've run out of credits to share. Feel free\n-to bring your own key! Meanwhile, The Wonderful Wizard of Oz is ready\n-to read, with its soundtrack and illustrations.\" The UI links the Oz\n-sentence to `CREDITS_OUT_LIBRARY_HREF` (`\"/\"`). Caption is the scene\n-title for scenes and the first words of the paragraph for passages,\n-built server-side.\n+`bad_request` with a friendly English message. Both `budget` and\n+`daily_budget` answer `MSG_CREDITS_OUT` (`core/images.ts`): the free\n+credits ran out, bring your own key, and meanwhile the Oz reader is\n+ready with its soundtrack and illustrations. It never says \"come back\n+tomorrow\". The UI links the Oz sentence via `CREDITS_OUT_LIBRARY_HREF`\n+(`\"/\"`). Caption is the scene title, or the paragraph's first words,\n+built server-side.\n","final_result":true,"kind":"output","task_id":"01a182c9-789b-7f33-83db-0b815bf4d994"},"kind":"task_lifecycle","run_stream":{"id":"01a182c7-21ae-7563-b8aa-8495f4c7e6b2","kind":"run"},"task_id":"01a182c9-789b-7f33-83db-0b815bf4d994","task_stream":{"id":"01a182c9-789b-7f33-83db-0b815bf4d994","kind":"task"}}}
